Ú;ÿ=d)Ωrëz<‹˙ÓºOëº˛„ƒ<§=L-∫ª|§·ªÄ"—;Èø$ºƒ£<8o*∏îeºîGHº8#º¿¶º?–B=€´<;ÌôºÈã≈<πÆç∫„)÷ºòëX<Ì^ª Àl=]<Ä<Œ—÷ª-ê¢<M,„;Ìª;Ω√g;ﬂE÷∫«
Æ<¢◊«<≥L∫¿vºE3	:x¬èªÜQ∏<—;ºÓíΩ˛J¨<ﬂﬂ≈<Ê€§ºëc»ºo·Ÿª‹<‚ë<È%µ<„¬Ó∫aÍr<óíØºdjê<ãºëbÒ:≥K«<Ø4ø;á+º•ºû<‹˙n<É(<®ÜºI{kºΩë∂ºa)=uºT£;É:∞:Àπ˜<çÊØ<îÆ/ΩBª…õª≥≤Æ8ÿ±µ<a©< Õö<≥ø<>8ºŒjÔ;˛MºZãàªîH<S\!<¢=ÿª“OFªP™“;∂ñ.;I}º{"title": "SOPLADOR ROSADO:The term \"Soplador Rosado\" refers to a classic phenotype of EPOC characterized by a specific body type and respiratory symptoms."}{"title": "OBESO AZULADO:The term \"Obeso Azulado\" refers to another classic phenotype of EPOC, indicating a different body type and associated symptoms."}{"title": "DEFECTO CELULAR:Cellular defect refers to abnormalities at the cellular level that can contribute to various health issues, including those seen in EPOC patients."}{"title": "D\u00c9FICIT DE ENERG\u00cdA:Energy deficit refers to a state where the energy intake is less than the energy expenditure, which can affect patients with chronic diseases like EPOC."}{"title": "ALTERACI\u00d3N DE M\u00daSCULOS RESPIRATORIOS:Alteration of respiratory muscles refers to changes in the function or structure of the muscles involved in breathing, often seen in EPOC patients."}{"title": "ALTERACI\u00d3N PAR\u00c9NQUIMA PULMONAR:Alteration of pulmonary parenchyma refers to changes in the lung tissue that can affect respiratory function, commonly observed in EPOC."}{"title": "DISFUNCI\u00d3N INMUNE:Immune dysfunction refers to the impaired immune response that can occur in patients with chronic diseases, including EPOC."}{"title": "INFECCI\u00d3N PULMONAR:Pulmonary infection refers to infections that affect the lungs, which can be a significant risk for patients with EPOC."}{"title": "MIOFIBRILLAS:Myofibrils are the basic rod-like units of a muscle cell, and their type and distribution can be affected in patients with EPOC."}{"title": "MASA \u00d3SEA:Bone mass refers to the amount of bone tissue in the body, which can be affected in patients with chronic diseases like EPOC."}{"title": "BODE INDEX:The BODE index is a multidimensional grading system used to assess the severity of EPOC, incorporating factors such as BMI, airway obstruction, dyspnea, and exercise capacity."}{"title": "MRC:The Medical Research Council (MRC) dyspnea scale is a tool used to measure the degree of breathlessness in patients."}{"title": "CIRCUMFERENCE OF ARM:The circumference of the arm is a simple measurement used to assess muscle mass and nutritional status in patients with EPOC."}{"title": "OBESITY PARADOX:The obesity paradox refers to the phenomenon where obesity may be associated with better outcomes in certain diseases, including EPOC, despite the general health risks of being overweight."}{"title": "GOLD STAGE:"}{"title": "HIPOXEMIA CR\u00d3NICA:Chronic hypoxemia is a condition characterized by low oxygen levels in the blood, which can complicate the health of patients with respiratory diseases"}{"title": "ATROFIA MUSCULAR:Atrofia muscular, or muscle atrophy, is a condition characterized by the loss of muscle mass. This phenomenon is particularly prevalent in patients with ELA (Amyotrophic Lateral Sclerosis) as well as those suffering from chronic respiratory diseases. In these patients, muscle wasting can be attributed to a combination of factors, including nutritional deficiencies and increased energy requirements, which lead to inactivity. The condition highlights the importance of addressing both nutritional needs and physical activity to mitigate the effects of muscle atrophy in affected individuals."}{"title": "BQ:BQ refers to Bronchiectasis, a condition characterized by the abnormal and permanent dilation of the bronchi, leading to chronic respiratory issues. This condition results in the airways of the lungs becoming abnormally widened, which causes a build-up of excess mucus, making the lungs more susceptible to infections. Additionally, Bronchiectasis, also known as Bronquiectasias, requires assessments of dietary and muscle function, highlighting its impact on overall health. The condition has been associated with respiratory rehabilitation, which can lead to improvements in exercise capacity and quality of life. Furthermore, the abnormal widening of the bronchi can also affect nutrition, indicating the multifaceted nature of this respiratory disorder."}{"title": "VALORACI\u00d3N:VALORACI\u00d3N refers to the comprehensive assessment of nutritional intake and status, which is essential for patient care in hospitals. This process includes evaluating a patient's attitude towards enteral nutrition, a critical aspect for their psychological and nutritional management. Additionally, VALORACI\u00d3N encompasses the assessment of dietary adherence and nutritional status specifically in patients with chronic diseases, highlighting its importance in managing their overall health and well-being."}{"title": "DINAMOMETR\u00cdA DE MANO:Dinamometr\u00eda de mano is a simple and cost-effective method to measure handgrip strength, correlating with muscle mass and nutritional status."}{"title": "PROTEIN-INDUCED DEFICIT OF VITAMIN K:PIDVK is a marker used to assess vitamin K deficiency, particularly in patients with chronic diseases like FQ."}{"title": "OSTEOCALCIN:Osteocalcin is a protein involved in bone metabolism and can indicate vitamin K status, relevant in chronic disease management."}{"title": "HEMOGLOBIN:"}{"title": "IPE:IPE, or Insuficiencia Pancre\u00e1tica Exocrina, refers to a medical condition characterized by exocrine pancreatic insufficiency, where the pancreas fails to produce sufficient digestive enzymes. This condition significantly impacts nutrient absorption, particularly in patients with cystic fibrosis, necessitating tailored dietary management and specific nutritional interventions. Additionally, monitoring of vitamin and mineral levels is crucial for individuals with IPE to ensure adequate nutrition and overall health."}{"title": "PROTEINA C REACTIVA:C-reactive protein is a marker of inflammation in the body, often measured to assess inflammatory conditions, including in patients with FQ."}{"title": "TNF-ALFA:Tumor necrosis factor-alpha is a cytokine involved in systemic inflammation, which may be relevant in the context of chronic diseases like FQ."}{"title": "DENSIDAD MINERAL OSEA:Bone mineral density is a measure of bone strength and is important for assessing osteoporosis risk, particularly in patients with FQ."}{"title": "Z-SCORE:The Z-score is a statistical measurement that serves multiple purposes in different contexts. It is primarily used to evaluate growth in children by comparing an individual's growth metrics to a reference population. Additionally, the Z-score is utilized in the medical field to assess bone density in patients with conditions such as cystic fibrosis (FQ), indicating how a specific value relates to the mean of a group. Overall, the Z-score provides a standardized way to understand how an individual compares to a broader population, whether in terms of growth or health metrics."}{"title": "CYSTIC FIBROSIS FOUNDATION:The Cystic Fibrosis Foundation is a non-profit organization dedicated to advancing research and care for individuals with cystic fibrosis. It focuses on funding research initiatives and providing essential support for those affected by the condition. Additionally, the foundation offers guidelines and recommendations for managing cystic fibrosis, which include dietary needs and supplementation, as well as comprehensive support for treatment and care management. Through its efforts, the Cystic Fibrosis Foundation plays a crucial role in improving the quality of life for individuals living with cystic fibrosis."}{"title": "BETACAROTENOS:Beta-carotene is a source of Vitamin A that may be safer for supplementation compared to retinol, especially in certain health conditions."}{"title": "MINERALES Y OLIGOELEMENTOS:Minerals and trace elements are essential nutrients that may need to be supplemented in various health conditions, particularly in patients with specific dietary deficiencies."}{"title": "HEPATOPAT\u00cdA SEVERA:Severe liver disease is a condition that may require careful management of vitamin supplementation, particularly Vitamin A and K."}{"title": "ANTIBIOTERAPIA PROLONGADA:Prolonged antibiotic therapy can impact nutrient absorption and may necessitate supplementation of vitamins and minerals."}{"title": "RESECCIONES COL\u00d3NICAS AMPLIAS:Extensive colon resections can lead to malabsorption issues, requiring careful nutritional support and supplementation."}{"title": "ENZYMES:Pancreatic enzymes are supplements that help cystic fibrosis patients with IPE to absorb fats effectively from their diet."}{"title": "SODIUM SUPPLEMENTATION:Sodium supplementation is recommended for cystic fibrosis patients, especially in specific age groups and conditions to prevent sodium deficiency."}{"title": "KREON 10000:Kreon 10000 is a pancreatic enzyme preparation available in Spain, containing 10,000 units of lipase per dose, used for patients with pancreatic insufficiency."}{"title": "KREON 25000:Kreon 25000 is a pancreatic enzyme preparation available in Spain, containing 25,000 units of lipase per dose, used for patients with pancreatic insufficiency."}{"title": "KREON 5000 GRANULADO:Kreon 5000 granulado is a pancreatic enzyme preparation available in Spain, containing 5,000 units of lipase per gram, used for patients with pancreatic insufficiency."}{"title": "AMILASA (ALFA):Alpha-amylase is an enzyme that helps digest carbohydrates, included in pancreatic enzyme preparations for patients with pancreatic insufficiency."}{"title": "PROTEASA:Protease is an enzyme that helps break down proteins in the digestive system, included in pancreatic enzyme preparations for patients with pancreatic insufficiency."}{"title": "PACIENTES CON PANCREATITIS CR\u00d3NICA:Patients with chronic pancreatitis often require pancreatic enzyme supplementation to aid in digestion and improve nutrient absorption."}{"title": "OLIVEIRA G:Oliveira G is a researcher known for significant contributions to the field of nutrition, particularly in relation to cystic fibrosis. They have focused on the nutritional aspects of the condition, exploring the importance of nutritional support for individuals with cystic fibrosis. Additionally, Oliveira G has investigated the effectiveness of various methods for estimating trends in home enteral nutrition, further emphasizing their commitment to improving nutritional care for patients. Through their work, Oliveira G has played a vital role in advancing the understanding of nutritional needs and support strategies in the context of cystic fibrosis."}{"title": "COLPAT\u00cdA FIBROSANTE:Fibrosing colonopathy is a potential complication associated with excessive doses of pancreatic enzymes in cystic fibrosis patients."}{"title": "DISTRIBUCI\u00d3N:Distribution refers to the method of administering pancreatic enzymes and ensuring they are effective in cystic fibrosis treatment."}{"title": "ADMINISTRACI\u00d3N:The term \"ADMINISTRACI\u00d3N\" encompasses the processes involved in providing essential medical care to patients, particularly those with specific health conditions. It includes the administration of pancreatic enzymes, which is vital for managing cystic fibrosis, a genetic disorder that affects the lungs and digestive system. Additionally, \"ADMINISTRACI\u00d3N\" refers to the methods of delivering enteral nutrition to patients, which can be done either continuously or intermittently, depending on the individual needs of the patient. This comprehensive approach to administration highlights the importance of tailored medical interventions in improving patient health outcomes."}{"title": "TURK D ET AL.:Author referenced in the guidelines for nutritional support in patients with pulmonary pathology, particularly in relation to fibrosis qu\u00edstica."}{"title": "AG ESENCIALES:Essential fatty acids are crucial nutrients that may be included in specialized formulas for patients with fibrosis qu\u00edstica."}{"title": "AG DE LA SERIE \u03a9-3:Omega-3 fatty acids are a type of essential fatty acid that may be beneficial in the dietary management of patients with fibrosis qu\u00edstica."}{"title": "FORMULAS ESPEC\u00cdFICAS PARA DIABETES:Specific formulas for diabetes are designed to provide appropriate nutrition for patients with both diabetes and fibrosis qu\u00edstica."}{"title": "FERREIRA ET AL.:Ferreira et al. are researchers who published a Cochrane review evaluating the effects of nutritional supplements in patients with EPOC."}{"title": "ALIMENTOS HIPERCAL\u00d3RICOS:Hypercaloric foods are those that provide a high number of calories, often used in dietary management for patients needing to increase caloric intake."}{"title": "FERREIRA:Ferreira is a researcher who conducted a meta-analysis on the effects of nutritional supplementation in patients with EPOC."}{"title": "SUPLEMENTO HIPERPROTEICO:Suplemento hiperproteico refers to a high-protein supplement that has been studied for its effects on patients with respiratory conditions, particularly in improving muscle mass and strength."}{"title": "SOCIEDAD ESPA\u00d1OLA DE MEDICINA INTENSIVA, CR\u00cdTICA Y UNIDADES CORONARIAS:The Sociedad Espa\u00f1ola de Medicina Intensiva, Cr\u00edtica y Unidades Coronarias (SEMICYUC) provides guidelines and recommendations for nutritional support in critically ill patients with respiratory failure."}{"title": "SOCIEDAD ESPA\u00d1OLA DE NUTRICI\u00d3N PARENTERAL Y ENTERAL:The Sociedad Espa\u00f1ola de Nutrici\u00f3n Parenteral y Enteral (SENPE) is an organization dedicated to establishing quality criteria for clinical nutrition. It plays a crucial role in providing recommendations for nutritional support specifically aimed at patients who require artificial nutrition. Through its efforts, SENPE aims to enhance the standards and practices related to parenteral and enteral nutrition in clinical settings."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME DE DISTR\u00c9S RESPIRATORIO DEL ADULTO:The S\u00edndrome de Distr\u00e9s Respiratorio del Adulto (SDRA) is a condition that requires specific nutritional support strategies to improve patient outcomes."}{"title": "AGENTES NUTRICIONALES:Agentes nutricionales refer to the specific nutrients and formulas used in nutritional support for patients with respiratory conditions."}{"title": "AG MONOINSATURADOS:AG monoinsaturados are specific fatty acids that can improve metabolic control in patients with concurrent diabetes or hyperglycemia."}{"title": "FALLO RESPIRATORIO AGUDO:"}{"title": "IVACAFTOR:Ivacaftor is a medication specifically designed to treat cystic fibrosis in patients who have certain mutations. It works by correcting the function of the RTFQ protein, which leads to improvements in lung function and nutritional status for these patients."}{"title": "LACTOBACILLUS GG:Lactobacillus GG is a strain of probiotic bacteria known for its potential health benefits. It has been shown to have a beneficial effect in the prevention of atopic dermatitis, although its effectiveness in addressing food allergies remains unproven. Additionally, Lactobacillus GG may help in reducing inflammation markers, further contributing to its reputation as a valuable probiotic."}{"title": "MUTACI\u00d3N GLY551ASP:Gly551Asp is a specific mutation associated with cystic fibrosis that affects the function of the RTFQ protein."}{"title": "BALEARIC ISLANDS:The Balearic Islands are a group of islands in Spain where improvements in newborn screening strategies for cystic fibrosis have been assessed."}{"title": "MULTIDISCIPLINARY REHABILITATION PROGRAM:A multidisciplinary rehabilitation program is designed to improve the functional capacity and quality of life of patients with chronic respiratory diseases."}{"title": "MACENZIE T:MacKenzie T is an author who contributed to research on the longevity of patients with cystic fibrosis."}{"title": "OLVEIRA G:Olveira G is a researcher and author specializing in the fields of cystic fibrosis and nutrition. They have conducted studies focused on various aspects of patient care, including providing recommendations for managing hyperglycemia in individuals receiving artificial nutrition. Additionally, Olveira G has investigated the issues of fat-free mass depletion and inflammation in patients with bronchiectasis. Their contributions to the literature include writing about the relationship between nutrition and cystic fibrosis, as well as studying the impact of parenteral nutrition on in-hospital mortality, with findings published in the journal Diabetes Care."}{"title": "MIRAVITLLES M:Miravitlles M is an author involved in research and guidelines related to EPOC and its treatment."}{"title": "DIETARY MODIFICATIONS:Dietary modifications refer to changes made to a patient's diet to improve their nutritional intake and overall health, particularly in chronic conditions like cystic fibrosis and EPOC."}{"title": "MART\u00cdNEZ-GARC\u00cdA M-A:Mart\u00ednez-Garc\u00eda M-A is a researcher involved in studies related to bronchiectasis and chronic obstructive pulmonary disease."}{"title": "DE LA ROSA CARRILLO D:De la Rosa Carrillo D is a researcher contributing to the understanding of bronchiectasis and its treatment."}{"title": "OLVEIRA C:Olveira C is a researcher who has made significant contributions to the field of bronchiectasis. They have analyzed the etiology of bronchiectasis in a cohort of patients and have co-authored studies related to this condition. Additionally, Olveira C has contributed to research focusing on the symptoms of depression and anxiety in patients with bronchiectasis, highlighting the multifaceted impact of this respiratory disease on mental health."}{"title": "\u00c1NGEL MART\u00cdNEZ M:\u00c1ngel Mart\u00ednez M is a researcher focused on bronchiectasis and its implications in respiratory diseases."}{"title": "GIR\u00d3N R:Gir\u00f3n R is a researcher who has contributed to studies on bronchiectasis."}{"title": "M\u00c1IZ L:M\u00e1iz L is a researcher involved in the study of bronchiectasis and its treatment."}{"title": "PATEL IS:Patel IS is a researcher who has studied bronchiectasis and its relationship with chronic obstructive pulmonary disease."}{"title": "DE BOECK K:De Boeck K is a researcher focused on cystic fibrosis and its diagnostic procedures."}{"title": "DERICHS N:Derichs N is a researcher involved in cystic fibrosis studies."}{"title": "FAJAC I:Fajac I is a researcher contributing to the understanding of cystic fibrosis."}{"title": "ELBORN JS:Elborn JS is a researcher who has reported on the care of adults with cystic fibrosis."}{"title": "J CYST FIBROS:The \"Journal of Cystic Fibrosis\" is a publication dedicated to disseminating research and guidelines pertaining to cystic fibrosis and its associated conditions. It specifically focuses on advancing knowledge and understanding of cystic fibrosis, providing valuable insights and information relevant to the field."}{"title": "AM J RESPIR CRIT CARE MED:American Journal of Respiratory and Critical Care Medicine publishes studies on respiratory diseases including bronchiectasis and cystic fibrosis."}{"title": "FACED SCORE:The FACED score is a multidimensional scoring system used to assess the severity of bronchiectasis."}{"title": "GASTROESOPHAGEAL REFLUX:Gastroesophageal reflux is a condition that can be prevalent in cystic fibrosis patients, impacting their lung health."}{"title": "DIRECT MEDICAL COSTS:Direct medical costs refer to the financial burden associated with the treatment of bronchiectasis and related conditions."}{"title": "EXACERBATIONS:Exacerbations are acute worsening of symptoms in chronic respiratory diseases, including bronchiectasis and COPD."}{"title": "MUNCK A:Munck A is one of the authors involved in the multicentre study on DIOS and constipation in cystic fibrosis."}{"title": "HAUSER B:Hauser B is one of the authors involved in the multicentre study on DIOS and constipation in cystic fibrosis."}{"title": "WALKOWIAK J:Walkowiak J is one of the authors involved in the multicentre study on DIOS and constipation in cystic fibrosis."}{"title": "DIOS:DIOS (Distal Intestinal Obstruction Syndrome) is a condition being studied in relation to cystic fibrosis."}{"title": "WHITAKER P:Whitaker P is an author who contributed to the research published in the Journal of Cystic Fibrosis."}{"title": "SERMET-GAUDELUS I:Sermet-Gaudelus I is an author involved in the European cystic fibrosis bone mineralisation guidelines."}{"title": "BIANCHI ML:Bianchi ML is an author involved in the European cystic fibrosis bone mineralisation guidelines."}{"title": "GARAB\u00c9DIAN M:Garab\u00e9dian M is an author involved in the European cystic fibrosis bone mineralisation guidelines."}{"title": "ARIS RM:Aris RM is an author involved in the European cystic fibrosis bone mineralisation guidelines."}{"title": "MORTON A:Morton A is an author involved in the European cystic fibrosis bone mineralisation guidelines."}{"title": "HARDIN DS:Hardin DS is an author involved in the European cystic fibrosis bone mineralisation guidelines."}{"title": "VENDRELL M:Vendrell M is an author who contributed to the diagnosis and treatment of bronchiectasis."}{"title": "DE GRACIA J:De Gracia J is an author who contributed to the diagnosis and treatment of bronchiectasis."}{"title": "MARTINEZ MA:Martinez MA is an author who contributed to the research on depression and anxiety symptoms in bronchiectasis."}{"title": "GIRON R:Giron R is an author who contributed to the research on nutritional state during COPD exacerbation."}{"title": "MAIZ L:Maiz L is a researcher and author who has made significant contributions to the field of respiratory health. They studied the prevalence of nontuberculous mycobacteria in patients with bronchiectasis, highlighting important aspects of this condition. Additionally, Maiz L contributed to research focused on the nutritional state during exacerbations of Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease (COPD), further emphasizing their commitment to understanding and improving health outcomes in respiratory diseases."}{"title": "SOLOR JJ:Soler JJ is an author who contributed to the research on malnutrition in outpatients with stable chronic obstructive pulmonary disease."}{"title": "SANCHEZ L:Sanchez L is an author who contributed to the research on malnutrition in outpatients with stable chronic obstructive pulmonary disease."}{"title": "PERPI\u00d1A M:Perpi\u00f1a M is an author who contributed to the research on malnutrition in outpatients with stable chronic obstructive pulmonary disease."}{"title": "BUDWEISER S:Budweiser S is an author who contributed to the research on nutritional depletion and respiratory impairment in chronic respiratory failure."}{"title": "MEYER K:Meyer K is an author who contributed to the research on nutritional depletion and respiratory impairment in chronic respiratory failure."}{"title": "J\u00d6RRES RA:J\u00f6rres RA is an author who contributed to the research on nutritional depletion and respiratory impairment in chronic respiratory failure."}{"title": "HEINEMANN F:Heinemann F is an author who contributed to the research on nutritional depletion and respiratory impairment in chronic respiratory failure."}{"title": "WILD PJ:Wild PJ is an author who contributed to the research on nutritional depletion and respiratory impairment in chronic respiratory failure."}{"title": "PFEIFER M:Pfeifer M is an author who contributed to the research on nutritional depletion and respiratory impairment in chronic respiratory failure."}{"title": "SCHOLS AM:Schols AM is an author who contributed to the European Respiratory Society statement on nutritional assessment and therapy in COPD."}{"title": "FERREIRA IM:Ferreira IM is a notable author and editor who has made significant contributions to the field of respiratory health, particularly in relation to Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease (COPD). They played a key role in the European Respiratory Society statement on nutritional assessment and therapy in COPD, highlighting the importance of nutrition in managing this condition. Additionally, Ferreira IM is actively involved as a researcher in the Cochrane Database of Systematic Reviews, where their focus is on nutritional supplementation for individuals with COPD. Through these efforts, Ferreira IM has contributed to advancing the understanding and treatment of nutritional needs in patients suffering from COPD."}{"title": "FRANSSEN FM:Franssen FM is an author who contributed to the European Respiratory Society statement on nutritional assessment and therapy in COPD."}{"title": "GOSKER HR:Gosker HR is an author who contributed to the European Respiratory Society statement on nutritional assessment and therapy in COPD."}{"title": "JANSSENS W:Janssens W is an author who contributed to the European Respiratory Society statement on nutritional assessment and therapy in COPD."}{"title": "CELL BR:Celli BR is a researcher and author recognized for significant contributions to the understanding of the Body-Mass Index (BMI) and its relationship with outcomes in chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD). Celli BR's work includes research on body composition and its impact on mortality rates among individuals suffering from COPD, highlighting the importance of these factors in managing the disease effectively."}{"title": "COTE CG:Cote CG is an author who contributed to the research on body composition and mortality in chronic obstructive pulmonary disease."}{"title": "MARIN JM:Marin JM is an author who contributed to the research on body composition and mortality in chronic obstructive pulmonary disease."}{"title": "CASANOVA C:Casanova C is an author who contributed to the research on body composition and mortality in chronic obstructive pulmonary disease."}{"title": "MONTES DE OCA:Montes de Oca is an author who contributed to the research on body composition and mortality in chronic obstructive pulmonary disease.)<|COMPLETE|>"}{"title": "AMERICAN THORACIC SOCIETY:The American Thoracic Society is a professional organization focused on advancing the clinical and scientific understanding of respiratory diseases, including chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD)."}{"title": "NUTRITIONAL DEPLETION:Nutritional depletion refers to a state where an individual lacks essential nutrients, which can significantly impact health, particularly in patients with chronic diseases like COPD."}{"title": "AMERICAN JOURNAL OF RESPIRATORY AND CRITICAL CARE MEDICINE:The American Journal of Respiratory and Critical Care Medicine is a peer-reviewed medical journal that publishes research on respiratory diseases, including COPD."}{"title": "BMC INFECTIOUS DISEASES:BMC Infectious Diseases is a peer-reviewed journal that publishes research on infectious diseases, including studies related to bronchiectasis."}{"title": "NUTRITION CARE GUIDELINES:Nutrition care guidelines provide recommendations for the nutritional management of patients with specific health conditions, including cystic fibrosis and COPD."}{"title": "VERMEEREN MAP:Vermeeren MAP is a researcher who studied the prevalence of nutritional depletion in patients with COPD."}{"title": "BOLTON CE:Bolton CE is a researcher who investigated the loss of fat-free mass and bone mineral density in COPD patients."}{"title": "SOLER-CATALU\u00d1A JJ:Soler-Catalu\u00f1a JJ is a researcher who studied the predictive value of mid-arm muscle area in COPD mortality."}{"title": "VILAR\u00d3 J:Vilar\u00f3 J is a researcher who focused on global muscle dysfunction as a risk factor for hospital readmission due to COPD exacerbations."}{"title": "ONEN ZP:Onen ZP is a researcher who analyzed factors related to mortality in patients with bronchiectasis."}{"title": "SPRUIT MA:Spruit MA is a researcher who contributed to the official statement on pulmonary rehabilitation for COPD patients."}{"title": "CEBRON LIPOVEC N:Cebron Lipovec N is a researcher who studied the prevalence of metabolic syndrome in COPD patients."}{"title": "DIEHL N:Diehl N is a researcher who focused on the prevalence of osteopenia and osteoporosis in patients with non-cystic fibrosis bronchiectasis."}{"title": "GRAAT-VERBOOM L:Graat-Verboom L is a researcher who conducted a systematic review on osteoporosis in COPD patients."}{"title": "SCHOLS AMWJ:"}{"title": "ESPEN-ESPGHAN-ECFS:ESPEN-ESPGHAN-ECFS is a guideline organization focused on nutrition care for individuals with cystic fibrosis."}{"title": "OLIVEIRA C:Oliveira C is a researcher engaged in studies concerning cystic fibrosis, particularly focusing on its dietary implications. This researcher has made significant contributions to understanding dietary intake in adults affected by cystic fibrosis, highlighting the importance of nutrition in managing the condition."}{"title": "EUROPEAN RESPIRATORY JOURNAL:Eur Respir J is a journal that publishes research on respiratory diseases, including studies related to chronic obstructive pulmonary disease and cystic fibrosis."}{"title": "ARCH BRONCONEUMOL:Arch Bronconeumol is a medical journal dedicated to the field of respiratory medicine. It publishes research on a variety of respiratory diseases, including chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD) and cystic fibrosis, as well as studies related to their treatment. The journal serves as a platform for disseminating important findings and advancements in the understanding and management of respiratory conditions."}{"title": "BMC PULM MED:BMC Pulm Med is a journal that publishes research on pulmonary medicine, including studies on anemia and its effects in COPD patients."}{"title": "ACOSTA E:Acosta E is a researcher who has worked on the effects of fatty acid supplementation in cystic fibrosis patients."}{"title": "ESP\u00cdLDORA F:Esp\u00edldora F is a researcher who has studied the impact of dietary supplementation in cystic fibrosis."}{"title": "GARRIDO-S\u00c1NCHEZ L:Garrido-S\u00e1nchez L is a researcher focused on the nutritional parameters in cystic fibrosis patients."}{"title": "GARC\u00cdA-ESCOBAR E:Garc\u00eda-Escobar E is a researcher who has contributed to studies on cystic fibrosis and nutrition."}{"title": "MARTINEZ-GARCIA MA:Martinez-Garcia MA is a researcher who has studied the association between bronchiectasis and systemic inflammation in cystic fibrosis patients."}{"title": "PERPINA-TORDERA M:Perpina-Tordera M is a researcher involved in studies related to cystic fibrosis and its complications."}{"title": "ROMAN-SANCHEZ P:Roman-Sanchez P is a researcher who has worked on the implications of systemic inflammation in cystic fibrosis."}{"title": "SOLER-CATALUNA JJ:Soler-Cataluna JJ is a researcher focused on the respiratory aspects of cystic fibrosis."}{"title": "NUTRITION CLINICAL MEDICINE:Nutrition Clinical Medicine is a journal that publishes research related to nutrition and its impact on health, including studies on cystic fibrosis."}{"title": "MULTIDISCIPLINARY RESPIRATORY MEDICINE:Multidisciplinary Respiratory Medicine is a journal that publishes research on various aspects of respiratory health, including studies on cystic fibrosis."}{"title": "NUTRITION IN CLINICAL PRACTICE:Nutrition in Clinical Practice is a journal that publishes research on nutrition and its clinical implications, including studies related to cystic fibrosis."}{"title": "JOURNAL OF CYSTIC FIBROSIS:The Journal of Cystic Fibrosis is a specialized journal that focuses on research and clinical practices related to cystic fibrosis."}{"title": "JOHN WILEY & SONS, LTD:John Wiley & Sons, Ltd is a global publishing company that specializes in academic publishing and educational materials."}{"title": "RESPIROLOGY:Respirology is a journal that publishes research on respiratory health and diseases."}{"title": "MART\u00cdNEZ-GONZ\u00c1LEZ MA:Mart\u00ednez-Gonz\u00e1lez MA is a researcher known for contributions to studies on the Mediterranean Diet and its health benefits."}{"title": "ENTERAL TUBE FEEDING:Enteral tube feeding is a method of delivering nutrition directly to the stomach or intestines through a tube. This approach is primarily utilized for patients who are unable to eat by mouth, including those with advanced dementia. It serves as a critical nutritional support system for individuals who cannot consume food orally, ensuring they receive the necessary nutrients for their health and well-being."}{"title": "CLINICAL AUDIT:Clinical audit involves systematic review and evaluation of clinical practices to improve patient care and outcomes, particularly in malnourished children with Cystic Fibrosis."}{"title": "DIETARY PATTERNS:Dietary patterns refer to the overall diet composition and food choices that can influence health outcomes, including respiratory diseases."}{"title": "MALNOURISHED CHILDREN:Malnourished children are those who do not receive adequate nutrition, which can lead to various health issues, including respiratory problems."}{"title": "SPANISH SOCIETY OF PULMONOLOGY AND THORACIC SURGERY:The Spanish Society of Pulmonology and Thoracic Surgery (SEPAR) is a professional organization focused on respiratory health and the management of pulmonary diseases in Spain."}{"title": "LATIN AMERICAN THORACIC SOCIETY:The Latin American Thoracic Society (ALAT) is a professional organization dedicated to the advancement of thoracic medicine and respiratory health in Latin America."}{"title": "ACUTE RESPIRATORY DISTRESS SYNDROME:Acute respiratory distress syndrome (ARDS) is a severe lung condition that occurs when fluid builds up in the air sacs, preventing proper oxygenation of the blood."}{"title": "EXERCISE TRAINING:Exercise training involves structured physical activity aimed at improving physical fitness and health, particularly beneficial for patients with chronic respiratory conditions."}{"title": "OMEGA-3 POLYUNSATURATED FATTY ACIDS:Omega-3 polyunsaturated fatty acids are essential fats that have been shown to have various health benefits, including anti-inflammatory properties, particularly in respiratory conditions."}{"title": "WOUTERS EFM:Wouters EFM is a researcher involved in the study of exercise capacity improvements in chronic obstructive pulmonary disease through dietary supplementation."}{"title": "CREUTZBERG EC:Creutzberg EC is a researcher who co-authored studies on respiratory rehabilitation and dietary interventions in chronic pulmonary disease."}{"title": "G\u00dcELL MR:G\u00fcell MR is a researcher who has worked on standards for quality care in respiratory rehabilitation for chronic pulmonary disease patients."}{"title": "LEE AL:Lee AL is a researcher who conducted a randomized controlled trial on the effects of exercise training in non-cystic fibrosis bronchiectasis."}{"title": "ANIWIDYANINGSIH W:Aniwidyaningsih W is a researcher who studied the impact of nutritional status on body functioning in chronic obstructive pulmonary disease."}{"title": "PONTES-ARRUDA A:Pontes-Arruda A is a researcher who investigated the effects of enteral feeding in mechanically ventilated patients with severe sepsis."}{"title": "GADEK JE:Gadek JE is a researcher who studied the effects of enteral feeding with omega-3 fatty acids in patients with acute respiratory distress syndrome."}{"title": "GARC\u00cdA DE ACILU M:Garc\u00eda de Acilu M is a researcher who reviewed the role of omega-3 polyunsaturated fatty acids in treating patients with acute respiratory distress syndrome."}{"title": "CHINUCK R:Chinuck R is a researcher who edited a systematic review on appetite stimulants for people with cystic fibrosis."}{"title": "ANDERSON JL:Anderson JL is a researcher who conducted a systematic review on the effects of probiotics on respiratory and nutritional outcomes in cystic fibrosis patients."}{"title": "QUON BS:Quon BS is a researcher focused on new and emerging targeted therapies for cystic fibrosis."}{"title": "PECES-BARBA G:Peces-Barba G is a researcher who contributed to the joint guidelines for the diagnosis and management of chronic obstructive pulmonary disease."}{"title": "BROEKHUIZEN R:"}{"title": "NUTRICI\u00d3N EN PACIENTES QUEMADOS Y TRAUMATOL\u00d3GICOS:The topic of nutrition in burned and trauma patients, focusing on the medical management and nutritional needs of these patients."}{"title": "TRAUMATISMO GRAVE:\"TRAUMATISMO GRAVE\" refers to severe trauma that can occur in various situations, including traumatic brain injury and polytrauma. Patients experiencing this condition require intensive medical and nutritional management due to the significant medical and social burdens associated with such injuries."}{"title": "PACIENTE QUEMADO:The \"PACIENTE QUEMADO\" refers to a burn patient who is suffering from severe burns and requires specific nutritional assessment and support. Due to the effects of burns on metabolism and nutrition, this patient necessitates specialized nutritional support and fluid therapy to aid in their recovery."}{"title": "MUSCULATURA ESQUEL\u00c9TICA:Skeletal muscle is affected in burn patients, leading to significant nutritional challenges and risks of malnutrition."}{"title": "DEPLECI\u00d3N INTRACELULAR:Intracellular depletion of amino acids occurs in burn patients, affecting their metabolic processes."}{"title": "TORONTO EQUATION:The Toronto equation is a formula suggested for calculating energy requirements in burned patients, based on regression analysis from indirect calorimetry studies."}{"title": "HARRIS-BENEDICT FORMULA:The Harris-Benedict formula is a method used to estimate an individual's basal metabolic rate and daily energy requirements."}{"title": "BURNED PATIENT:A burned patient is an individual who has sustained burns and may require specialized nutritional support and medical care."}{"title": "ESPEN 2013:"}{"title": "EDMAS GENERALIZADOS:Generalized edema is a common condition in burn patients due to massive fluid infusion, affecting various body systems."}{"title": "\u00cdLEO PARAL\u00cdTICO:\u00cdleo paral\u00edtico es una condici\u00f3n que afecta la funci\u00f3n gastrointestinal, caracterizada por la falta de movimiento en los intestinos. Esta condici\u00f3n puede desarrollarse en pacientes con quemaduras y, en algunos casos, puede permitir el uso de nutrici\u00f3n enteral a bajo flujo. El \u00edleo paral\u00edtico a menudo se asocia con una sobrecarga de fluidos, lo que contribuye a la disminuci\u00f3n de la motilidad intestinal."}{"title": "F\u00d3RMULA DE PARKLAND:The Parkland formula is a method used to calculate the initial fluid resuscitation volume for burn patients based on their weight and burn surface area."}{"title": "GU\u00cdAS DE SOCIEDADES INTERNACIONALES:International societies provide guidelines for the management and treatment of critically ill patients, including those with burns."}{"title": "REDOXS:The REDOXS study investigated the effects of glutamine (Gln) supplementation in critically ill patients, comparing enteral and parenteral administration methods."}{"title": "BURNED PATIENTS:BURNED PATIENTS are individuals who have suffered burns and require specialized nutritional support due to their unique metabolic needs. This specialized care is essential to aid in their recovery and to address the specific challenges posed by their injuries."}{"title": "NUTRITION PARENTERAL:Parenteral nutrition (NP) is a method of delivering nutrients directly into the bloodstream, often used when enteral feeding is not possible."}{"title": "PROPOFOL:A medication that contains lipids and is used in the administration of parenteral nutrition"}{"title": "L-GLN:A supplement proposed for use in parenteral nutrition, though its general recommendation is still under debate"}{"title": "SOCIEDAD ESPA\u00d1OLA DE MEDICINA INTENSIVA CR\u00cdTICA Y UNIDADES CORONARIAS:The Sociedad Espa\u00f1ola de Medicina Intensiva Cr\u00edtica y Unidades Coronarias (SEMICYUC) is an organization focused on critical care medicine and guidelines for the treatment of critically ill patients, including those with severe burns."}{"title": "GARC\u00cdA DE LORENZO:Garc\u00eda de Lorenzo is an author who contributed to the recommendations for nutritional support and metabolic management of critically ill patients, particularly burn patients."}{"title": "MATEOS A:Mateos A is an author who collaborated on the recommendations for nutritional support and metabolic management of critically ill patients, particularly burn patients."}{"title": "NUTRICI\u00d3N EN PACIENTES QUEMADOS:A topic of discussion and guidelines regarding nutritional management for patients who have suffered severe burns."}{"title": "CUIDADOS NUTRICIONALES:Nutritional care practices aimed at supporting critically ill patients, particularly those with severe burns."}{"title": "SCOTTISH INTERCOLLEGIATE GUIDELINES NETWORK:The Scottish Intercollegiate Guidelines Network (SIGN) is an organization dedicated to developing evidence-based clinical practice guidelines for the National Health Service (NHS) in Scotland. SIGN plays a crucial role in enhancing healthcare practices by providing a systematic approach to clinical guidelines. Additionally, the organization has established a classification system for these guidelines, ensuring that they are organized and accessible for healthcare professionals. Through its efforts, SIGN aims to improve the quality of care and health outcomes for patients in Scotland."}{"title": "AGENCY FOR HEALTH CARE POLICY AND RESEARCH:The Agency for Health Care Policy and Research is a U.S. agency that supports research to improve the quality of healthcare."}{"title": "GRADE SYSTEM:The GRADE system is a framework for rating the quality of evidence and strength of recommendations in clinical guidelines."}{"title": "PACIENTES CON TRAUMATISMO GRAVE:Patients with severe trauma who require specialized medical care and nutritional support."}{"title": "JADAD SCALE:The Jadad scale is a tool used to assess the quality of clinical trials, particularly in terms of randomization and blinding."}{"title": "HYPERCATABOLISM:Hypercatabolism refers to the accelerated breakdown of body tissues, often occurring in severe trauma or illness."}{"title": "PROTEIN-ENERGY MALNUTRITION:Protein-energy malnutrition is a form of malnutrition characterized by inadequate protein and energy intake, which can occur in critically ill patients."}{"title": "NUTRITIONAL THERAPY IN MAJOR BURNS:"}{"title": "ASOCIACI\u00d3N AMERICANA DE NEUROCIRUG\u00cdA:The Asociaci\u00f3n Americana de Neurocirug\u00eda provides guidelines for the nutritional support of patients with traumatic brain injuries (TCE)."}{"title": "AMINO\u00c1CIDOS RAMIFICADOS:AMINO\u00c1CIDOS RAMIFICADOS, also known as branched-chain amino acids (BCAAs), are supplements commonly utilized by athletes to enhance muscle recovery and performance. Additionally, BCAAs are employed in intravenous supplementation for patients in a vegetative state, aiming to improve their disability scores."}{"title": "INFECCIONES NOSOCOMIALES:INFECCIONES NOSOCOMIALES refer to hospital-acquired infections that occur in a healthcare setting. These infections have been the subject of studies aimed at evaluating the effectiveness of immunonutrition as a potential intervention. Research indicates that specific nutritional strategies can help reduce the incidence of nosocomial infections, highlighting the importance of nutrition in the management and prevention of these infections within hospitals."}{"title": "BURNS:Burns refer to injuries caused by heat, chemicals, electricity, or radiation, leading to damage to the skin and other tissues, often requiring specialized nutritional management for recovery."}{"title": "DENT DL:Dent DL is a researcher involved in studies related to immunonutrition and its effects on critically ill patients, including those with burns."}{"title": "J TRAUMA:J Trauma is a medical journal that focuses on publishing research related to trauma and emergency medicine. It encompasses a wide range of topics within trauma care, including studies on enteral feeding and burn injuries. The journal serves as a platform for disseminating important findings and advancements in the field of trauma care, contributing to the ongoing development of best practices in emergency medicine."}{"title": "J TRACE ELEM MED BIOL:J Trace Elem Med Biol is a journal focusing on trace elements in medicine and biology."}{"title": "J BURN CARE RES:J Burn Care Res is a journal dedicated to research on burn care and rehabilitation."}{"title": "J HUM NUTR DIET:J Hum Nutr Diet is a journal that focuses on human nutrition and dietetics."}{"title": "PHARMACOTHERAPY:Pharmacotherapy is a journal dedicated to the study of drug therapy and its effects. It serves as a platform for research and discussions related to the various aspects of pharmacological treatments."}{"title": "NUTRICI\u00d3N EN LA ENFERMEDAD TRAUM\u00c1TICA:A significant event discussing nutrition in traumatic conditions and critically burned patients."}{"title": "GUIDELINES FOR SPECIALIZED NUTRITIONAL SUPPORT:An event that outlines guidelines for nutritional and metabolic support in critically ill patients."}{"title": "SELEEN IN CRITICALLY ILL PATIENTS:A study focusing on the role of selenium in critically ill patients with systemic inflammatory response."}{"title": "OXANDROLONE TREATMENT:A treatment event involving the use of oxandrolone in adults with severe thermal injury."}{"title": "EARLY ENTERAL NUTRITION:A systematic review event comparing early versus late enteral nutritional support in burn injury."}{"title": "MILLER JT:Miller JT is a researcher involved in the study of oxandrolone treatment in burn patients."}{"title": "HERNDON DN:Herndon DN is a researcher and author who has made significant contributions to the fields of nutrition and burn care. He has been actively involved in studies that focus on these areas, enhancing the understanding and treatment of burn injuries. Additionally, Herndon DN played a role in formulating recommendations from the North American Surgical Nutrition Summit, further emphasizing his expertise and commitment to advancing nutritional practices in surgical care."}{"title": "WASIAK J:Wasiak J is a researcher who has conducted systematic reviews on nutritional support in burn injuries."}{"title": "BARBOSA E:Barbosa E is a researcher involved in studies on vitamin supplementation in burned children."}{"title": "CRITICALLY ILL PATIENTS:Patients who are in a critical condition and require intensive medical care, including nutritional support."}{"title": "TRAUMATIC BRAIN INJURY:An event that involves severe brain injury, often requiring specialized nutritional management."}{"title": "SYSTEMIC INFLAMMATORY RESPONSE:A condition that can occur in critically ill patients, affecting their nutritional needs and management."}{"title": "DOUBLE-BLIND STUDY:A type of clinical trial where neither the participants nor the researchers know who is receiving a particular treatment, used in nutritional studies."}{"title": "COMPLEJO ASISTENCIAL UNIVERSITARIO:The Complejo Asistencial Universitario is a university hospital complex located in Le\u00f3n, Spain. It serves as a comprehensive healthcare institution that offers a wide range of medical services and educational opportunities. The facility is particularly noted for its involvement in the treatment and nutritional support of patients with neurological diseases. Additionally, it provides specialized services in various medical fields, including endocrinology and neurology, making it a vital resource for both patient care and medical education in the region."}{"title": "TANIA RAMOS MART\u00cdNEZ:Dr. Tania Ramos Mart\u00ednez is a healthcare professional specializing in diet-drug interactions. She is a resident physician in the Endocrinology and Nutrition section at the Complejo Asistencial Universitario in Le\u00f3n. In addition to her clinical work, she is also an author who contributes to the field of diet and drug interactions, furthering the understanding of how dietary factors can influence medication efficacy and safety."}{"title": "MAR\u00cdA DOLORES BALLESTEROS POMAR:Dr. Mar\u00eda Dolores Ballesteros Pomar is a healthcare professional specializing in Endocrinology and Nutrition at the Complejo Asistencial Universitario in Le\u00f3n. She is associated with the Service of Endocrinology and Nutrition, where she contributes to evidence-based nutrition practices. As a specialist in nutrition and hydration, Dr. Ballesteros Pomar plays a significant role in providing expert care and guidance in her field."}{"title": "ADRI\u00c1N AR\u00c9S LUQUE:Adri\u00e1n Ar\u00e9s Luque is a healthcare professional affiliated with the Service of Neurology at the Complejo Asistencial Universitario in Le\u00f3n. He is involved in the Secci\u00f3n de Neurolog\u00eda, where he contributes to evidence-based medical practices, enhancing the quality of care provided in the field of neurology."}{"title": "NUTRICI\u00d3N ENTERAL DOMICILIARIA:\"NUTRICI\u00d3N ENTERAL DOMICILIARIA\" refers to a form of home nutritional therapy designed for patients who can digest food but are unable to obtain sufficient nutrients through oral intake. This specific type of home artificial nutrition involves delivering nutrients directly to the stomach or intestine, making it a crucial method for providing nutritional support to patients in their homes. It is particularly beneficial for individuals with neurological diseases and is a significant aspect of pediatric care, facilitating the early reintegration of children into their families while ensuring they receive necessary nutritional support.\n\nHome enteral nutrition (NED) encompasses the provision of nutrition through enteral means, which has been documented in various registries over the years. It serves patients with special nutritional needs, including those with specific medical conditions that hinder their ability to consume adequate nutrition through regular food. The approach has been evaluated for its cost-effectiveness and its impact on health outcomes, highlighting its importance in managing the nutritional needs of patients at home."}{"title": "AMERICAN SOCIETY FOR PARENT:The American Society for Parent is an organization that provides guidelines for nutritional support in patients requiring artificial nutrition."}{"title": "ENFERMEDAD VASCULAR CEREBRAL:Enfermedad Vascular Cerebral, tambi\u00e9n conocida como enfermedad cerebrovascular, es una condici\u00f3n que afecta el suministro de sangre al cerebro. Esta enfermedad puede resultar en complicaciones significativas, como la disfasia y la desnutrici\u00f3n, especialmente despu\u00e9s de un accidente cerebrovascular. Los problemas de salud y nutrici\u00f3n en los pacientes son comunes debido a la interrupci\u00f3n del flujo sangu\u00edneo, lo que resalta la importancia de una atenci\u00f3n adecuada y oportuna para mitigar sus efectos."}{"title": "BRONCOASPIRACI\u00d3N:BRONCOASPIRACI\u00d3N refers to a medical condition characterized by the inhalation of food, liquid, or vomit into the lungs. This condition often occurs in patients with dysphagia, a swallowing disorder, and poses significant health risks, particularly during enteral feeding. The entry of these substances into the lungs can lead to serious complications, including pneumonia and other infections. Therefore, bronchoaspiration is a critical concern in medical settings, especially for vulnerable patients who may have difficulty swallowing."}{"title": "NEUMON\u00cdAS:Pneumonia is a serious infection that can occur as a result of bronchoaspiration, with a high mortality rate among affected patients."}{"title": "INFECCI\u00d3N:Infecci\u00f3n refers to the invasion and multiplication of microorganisms in body tissues, representing a significant health concern, particularly in patients with catheters. It is the most common complication associated with the use of central venous catheters, which can lead to either local or systemic infections. Patients receiving parenteral nutrition are especially at risk for developing infections related to these catheters. Additionally, individuals who are immunosuppressed, such as those who have undergone hematopoietic transplants, are also vulnerable to infections due to their weakened immune systems. Furthermore, infections can arise as complications from dysphagia and malnutrition, contributing to increased morbidity in affected patients. Overall, the risk of infection is a critical consideration in the management of patients with various medical conditions and interventions."}{"title": "INMUNODEPRESI\u00d3N:INMUNODEPRESI\u00d3N refers to a medical condition characterized by a weakened immune system, which can result from various factors, including malnutrition and cancer treatments. This state of immunodepression leads to a less effective immune response, making individuals more susceptible to infections and other health complications. Specifically, in the context of cancer patients, malnutrition and dysphagia (difficulty swallowing) are significant contributors to this condition, further exacerbating the challenges faced by those affected."}{"title": "MALA CICATRIZACI\u00d3N:Poor healing is a condition that can occur due to malnutrition, which may be linked to dysphagia in patients."}{"title": "TEST DEL AGUA DE DEPIPPO:The DePippo water test is a clinical assessment used to evaluate swallowing ability by administering water to the patient and observing for signs of aspiration."}{"title": "FIBROSCOPIA:Fibroscopy is an invasive procedure that allows direct visualization of the swallowing process and assessment of pharyngeal mobility and sensitivity."}{"title": "EVALUACI\u00d3N DE SENSIBILIDAD FAR\u00cdNGEA:Pharyngeal sensitivity evaluation is a clinical assessment used to determine the ability to swallow safely and detect dysphagia."}{"title": "S\u00cdNTOMAS Y SIGNOS DE ATRAGANTAMIENTO:Symptoms and signs of choking are critical indicators of dysphagia, requiring immediate assessment and intervention."}{"title": "TEST GUSS:The GUSS (Gugging Swallowing Screen) is a screening tool used to assess swallowing ability and identify dysphagia in patients."}{"title": "EQUIPOS M\u00c9DICOS Y DE ENFERMER\u00cdA:"}{"title": "ESTUDIO FOOD 1:Investigaci\u00f3n que eval\u00faa la efectividad de la administraci\u00f3n sistem\u00e1tica de suplementos orales en pacientes que han sufrido un ictus"}{"title": "ESTUDIO FOOD 2:Investigaci\u00f3n que analiza el inicio de la nutrici\u00f3n enteral y su impacto en la mortalidad y complicaciones en pacientes con ictus"}{"title": "\u00daLCERAS DE PRESI\u00d3N:Complicaci\u00f3n que puede surgir en pacientes con enfermedad vascular cerebral, afectando sus requerimientos nutricionales"}{"title": "ALIMENTOS DE TEXTURA MODIFICADA:Alimentos dise\u00f1ados para facilitar la alimentaci\u00f3n de pacientes con disfagia, generalmente de alta densidad cal\u00f3rica e hiperproteicos"}{"title": "HIDROELECTROL\u00cdTICO:Balance hidroelectrol\u00edtico refers to the maintenance of electrolyte levels in patients, which is crucial for their overall health, especially in those receiving enteral nutrition."}{"title": "M\u00daSCULOS RESPIRATORIOS:M\u00fasculos respiratorios are the muscles involved in breathing, which can be affected by ELA and its nutritional implications."}{"title": "HOSPITAL BELLVITGE:Hospital Bellvitge is a medical institution that conducts studies on the management of patients with ELA, demonstrating the benefits of a multidisciplinary approach in patient care."}{"title": "ELA:Esclerosis Lateral Amiotr\u00f3fica (ELA) is a progressive neurodegenerative disease that affects motor neurons, leading to muscle atrophy and various complications, including dysphagia."}{"title": "IMMUNE SYSTEM DYSFUNCTION:Immune system dysfunction occurs in ELA patients, increasing the risk of infections and complicating their overall health status."}{"title": "BODY COMPOSITION:Body composition refers to the proportion of fat and non-fat mass in the body, and it plays a crucial role in the nutritional management of patients, particularly those with esophageal cancer (ELA patients). Body composition analysis in these patients helps determine the levels of fat, lean mass, and hydration, which are essential for tailoring effective nutritional strategies. Additionally, it is important to note that body composition can change significantly in patients undergoing treatment for esophageal cancer, highlighting the need for ongoing assessment and adjustment of nutritional plans."}{"title": "HIGI\u00c9NICO-DIET\u00c9TICAS:Las medidas higi\u00e9nico-diet\u00e9ticas son pr\u00e1cticas recomendadas para optimizar la ingesta nutricional en pacientes con esclerosis lateral amiotr\u00f3fica."}{"title": "SUPORTE NUTRICIONAL:SUPORTE NUTRICIONAL se refiere a un conjunto de intervenciones dise\u00f1adas para mejorar el estado nutricional de los pacientes, especialmente aquellos que est\u00e1n en riesgo de desnutrici\u00f3n. Estas intervenciones son fundamentales para asegurar que los pacientes reciban la nutrici\u00f3n adecuada necesaria para su recuperaci\u00f3n y bienestar."}{"title": "COBALAMINA (B12):La cobalamina, o vitamina B12, es esencial para la mielinizaci\u00f3n, un proceso cr\u00edtico para la funci\u00f3n neuronal."}{"title": "PIRIDOXINA (B6):La piridoxina, o vitamina B6, es importante para la s\u00edntesis de reguladores bioqu\u00edmicos que afectan la funci\u00f3n cerebral."}{"title": "\u00c1CIDO F\u00d3LICO (B9):El \u00e1cido f\u00f3lico, o vitamina B9, es crucial para el desarrollo fetal del sistema nervioso central."}{"title": "FRAMINGHAM STUDY:The Framingham Study is a long-term, ongoing cardiovascular cohort study of residents of the town of Framingham, Massachusetts, which has provided significant insights into the relationship between omega-3 levels and cognitive function."}{"title": "OMEGA-3:Omega-3 refers to a group of polyunsaturated fatty acids that are important for human health, particularly in relation to cognitive function and inflammation."}{"title": "EATING BEHAVIOR SCALE:The Eating Behavior Scale is a tool used to assess the ability of individuals, particularly those with cognitive impairments, to eat independently."}{"title": "L-DOPA:L-DOPA es un medicamento utilizado en el tratamiento de la enfermedad de Parkinson que requiere una absorci\u00f3n adecuada para ser efectivo."}{"title": "GRUPO NADYA-SENPE:The GRUPO NADYA-SENPE is a Spanish organization dedicated to home enteral nutrition. It functions as a working group that focuses on artificial nutrition in the home setting, engaging in various reports and studies related to enteral nutrition. Through its efforts, GRUPO NADYA-SENPE aims to enhance the understanding and implementation of enteral nutrition practices in Spain."}{"title": "ENFERMEDAD DE MOTONEURONA:"}{"title": "FOOD TRIAL COLLABORATION:The FOOD Trial Collaboration is a group that conducts research on nutritional status and its impact on stroke outcomes."}{"title": "DENNIS MS:Dennis MS is a researcher involved in the FOOD trial and studies related to stroke management."}{"title": "NATIONAL COLLABORATING CENTRE FOR CHRONIC CONDITIONS:This organization provides clinical guidelines for the diagnosis and management of chronic conditions, including stroke."}{"title": "LONDON:London is the location of the Royal College of Physicians, which published guidelines for stroke management."}{"title": "AMYOTROPHIC LATERAL SCLEROSIS:Amyotrophic lateral sclerosis (ALS) is a progressive neurodegenerative disease that primarily affects nerve cells in the brain and spinal cord. This neurological condition specifically targets motor neurons, leading to a decline in muscle control and function. ALS is a significant focus of clinical management and ongoing research, as advancements in understanding and treating the disease continue to evolve."}{"title": "ACUTE STROKE:Acute stroke is a medical condition that requires immediate attention and is the focus of multiple studies regarding nutritional status and management."}{"title": "EATING ASSESSMENT TOOL (EAT-10):The Eating Assessment Tool (EAT-10) is a validated tool used for screening dysphagia in patients, particularly relevant in stroke management."}{"title": "ENMC INTERNATIONAL WORKSHOP:The 135th ENMC International Workshop focused on nutrition in amyotrophic lateral sclerosis, held from March 18-20, 2005, in Naarden, The Netherlands."}{"title": "PREDIMED STUDY INVESTIGATORS:The PREDIMED Study Investigators conducted research on the effects of the Mediterranean diet on cardiovascular disease prevention."}{"title": "NUTRITIONAL MANAGEMENT IN MND/ALS:Nutritional management in motor neuron disease (MND) and amyotrophic lateral sclerosis (ALS) focuses on dietary strategies to improve patient outcomes."}{"title": "NUTRITION IN AMYOTROPHIC LATERAL SCLEROSIS:Nutrition in amyotrophic lateral sclerosis refers to dietary interventions aimed at managing symptoms and improving quality of life for ALS patients."}{"title": "NUTRITIONAL SUPPORT IN NEUROLOGICAL DISEASES:Nutritional support in patients with neurological diseases involves dietary strategies to enhance health and manage symptoms."}{"title": "JIM\u00c9NEZ GARC\u00cdA I:Jim\u00e9nez Garc\u00eda I is a researcher who contributed to the study of nutritional management in ALS patients."}{"title": "ANDERSEN PM:Andersen PM is a researcher involved in the clinical guidelines for the management of amyotrophic lateral sclerosis."}{"title": "LUDOLPH AC:Ludolph AC is a researcher who has contributed to the understanding and management of amyotrophic lateral sclerosis."}{"title": "BULBAR SYMPTOMS:Bulbar symptoms in amyotrophic lateral sclerosis refer to difficulties in speech and swallowing, which require specific diagnosis and treatment strategies."}{"title": "PREDIMED-NAVARRA:The PREDIMED-NAVARRA trial is a randomized study that investigates the effects of the Mediterranean diet on cognition."}{"title": "OMEGA-3 FATTY ACID:Omega-3 fatty acids are essential nutrients that have garnered attention for their potential benefits in preventing dementia and enhancing cognitive performance."}{"title": "OMEGAD STUDY:The OmegAD study investigates the effects of docosahexaenoic acid-rich n-3 fatty acid supplementation on cytokine release and cognitive health."}{"title": "FRAMINGHAM HEART STUDY:The Framingham Heart Study is a long-term, ongoing cardiovascular cohort study that has also explored the relationship between diet and cognitive health."}{"title": "DANIEL ANTONIO DE LUIS ROM\u00c1N:Daniel Antonio De Luis Rom\u00e1n is a distinguished medical professional specializing in advanced nutritional support, particularly in the areas of enteral and parenteral nutrition. He is associated with the Hospital Cl\u00ednico Universitario de Valladolid and serves as the Executive Director of the Instituto de Endocrinolog\u00eda y Nutrici\u00f3n. His contributions to the field of clinical nutrition are significant, as he has co-authored studies on water metabolism in patients receiving artificial nutrition and has researched immunonutrition in artificial nutritional support.\n\nIn addition to his work in general nutrition, Daniel Antonio De Luis Rom\u00e1n has focused on the nutritional needs of patients undergoing head and neck tumor surgery, demonstrating his expertise in this specialized area. His extensive involvement in various topics related to nutrition underscores his commitment to advancing knowledge and practices in the field, making him a key figure in the study and application of nutritional support in clinical settings."}{"title": "EMILIA G\u00d3MEZ HOYOS:Emilia G\u00f3mez Hoyos is a medical professional and researcher specializing in nutrition, with a particular focus on enteral and parenteral nutrition. She has made significant contributions to the field of immunonutrition in artificial nutritional support, emphasizing its importance in clinical settings. Her research extends to the study of nutrition in oncology, where she has specifically investigated the nutritional needs of patients with head and neck tumors. Additionally, Emilia is recognized as an author in the field of clinical nutrition, contributing to various studies, including one on water metabolism in patients receiving artificial nutrition. Through her work, Emilia G\u00f3mez Hoyos has established herself as a key figure in advancing knowledge and practices related to nutritional support in medical care."}{"title": "JUAN JOS\u00c9 L\u00d3PEZ G\u00d3MEZ:Juan Jos\u00e9 L\u00f3pez G\u00f3mez is a distinguished medical professional specializing in nutrition, particularly in the areas of enteral and parenteral nutrition. He has made significant contributions to the field through his research and clinical practice. L\u00f3pez G\u00f3mez is a co-author of a study focused on water metabolism in patients receiving artificial nutrition and has also contributed to research on immunonutrition in artificial nutritional support. His expertise extends to oncology nutrition, where he is involved in the nutritional management of patients undergoing treatment for head and neck tumors. Overall, Juan Jos\u00e9 L\u00f3pez G\u00f3mez is recognized for his comprehensive work in clinical nutrition, with a particular emphasis on enteral nutrition and its various indications."}{"title": "BEATRIZ TORRES TORRES:Beatriz Torres Torres is a distinguished medical professional and researcher specializing in clinical nutrition, particularly in the context of artificial nutrition. She has co-authored a study on water metabolism in patients receiving artificial nutrition and has contributed significantly to research on immunonutrition in artificial nutritional support. Her expertise extends to both enteral and parenteral nutrition, where she has been actively involved in both study and practice. Additionally, Beatriz Torres Torres focuses on oncology nutrition, with a particular emphasis on the nutritional needs of patients with head and neck tumors. Through her work, she has established herself as a key figure in the field of clinical nutrition and parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "NUTRITION IN ONCOLOGY:Nutrition in Oncology is a specialized field of study that concentrates on the nutritional needs and interventions for cancer patients. This area of research is particularly important for individuals undergoing treatments such as hematopoietic stem cell transplants, as it addresses the unique dietary requirements and challenges faced by these patients during their treatment journey."}{"title": "ARTIFICIAL ENTERAL NUTRITION:Artificial enteral nutrition refers to the provision of nutrients through a feeding tube, which is critical for patients unable to eat by mouth."}{"title": "NEUROPROTECTIVE STRATEGIES:Neuroprotective strategies are approaches aimed at protecting the brain from injury or degeneration, often involving dietary interventions."}{"title": "YAIZA L\u00d3PEZ PLASENCIA:Yaiza L\u00f3pez Plasencia is a healthcare professional and medical expert specializing in the assessment and nutritional support of oncology patients. She plays a crucial role in providing nutritional guidance and support tailored to the needs of individuals undergoing cancer treatment, ensuring they receive the necessary care to enhance their overall health and well-being during this challenging time."}{"title": "DUNIA MARRERO ARENCIBIA:Dunia Marrero Arencibia is a healthcare professional specializing in oncology nutrition, where she plays a vital role in providing nutritional support to oncology patients. Her expertise in this field enables her to contribute significantly to the well-being and recovery of individuals undergoing cancer treatment."}{"title": "CARLOS RODR\u00cdGUEZ P\u00c9REZ:Carlos Rodr\u00edguez P\u00e9rez is a healthcare professional who specializes in the nutritional support and assessment of oncology patients. His work focuses on ensuring that patients undergoing cancer treatment receive appropriate nutritional care to support their health and recovery."}{"title": "ELENA GARC\u00cdA FERN\u00c1NDEZ:Dr. Elena Garc\u00eda Fern\u00e1ndez is a medical professional specializing in nutritional support for hematological patients. She is actively involved in the fields of nutrition and endocrinology at Hospital Universitario 12 de Octubre, where she applies her expertise to enhance the health and well-being of her patients."}{"title": "M.\u00c1NGELES VALERO ZANUY:M. \u00c1ngeles Valero Zanuy is a medical professional specializing in nutritional support for patients undergoing bone marrow transplants."}{"title": "HOSPITAL CL\u00cdNICO UNIVERSITARIO:The Hospital Cl\u00ednico Universitario is a prominent medical institution located in Valladolid, Spain. It serves as a clinical hospital that provides a wide range of medical services and is actively involved in research. The hospital specializes in various fields, including oncology nutrition, endocrinology, and clinical nutrition. Additionally, it conducts research and clinical practices related to pediatric gastroenterology and nutrition. Overall, the Hospital Cl\u00ednico Universitario is recognized for its comprehensive approach to healthcare, integrating both clinical services and research initiatives to enhance patient care and medical knowledge."}{"title": "CENTRO DE INVESTIGACI\u00d3N DE ENDOCRINOLOG\u00cdA Y NUTRICI\u00d3N:The \"Centro de Investigaci\u00f3n de Endocrinolog\u00eda y Nutrici\u00f3n\" is a dedicated research center that specializes in the fields of endocrinology and nutrition. This institution is actively involved in conducting research aimed at advancing knowledge and understanding in these areas, contributing to the broader scientific community's efforts to address health issues related to hormonal and nutritional factors."}{"title": "SOPORTE NUTRICIONAL EN EL PACIENTE CON CIRUG\u00cdA ONCOL\u00d3GICA DE EST\u00d3MAGO, ES\u00d3FAGO Y P\u00c1NCREAS:A medical topic addressing nutritional support for patients undergoing oncological surgeries of the stomach, esophagus, and pancreas."}{"title": "VALORACI\u00d3N Y SOPORTE NUTRICIONAL EN EL PACIENTE ONCOL\u00d3GICO:A medical topic that emphasizes the assessment and nutritional support necessary for oncology patients."}{"title": "SOPORTE NUTRICIONAL EN EL PACIENTE HEMATOL\u00d3GICO:A medical topic focusing on nutritional support for hematological patients, particularly those undergoing bone marrow transplants and dealing with graft-versus-host disease."}{"title": "DIFICULTADES NUTRICIONALES:A medical topic discussing the nutritional difficulties faced by patients with head and neck tumors, including issues like dysphagia."}{"title": "ALTERACIONES CICATRIZ:A medical topic discussing the complications related to healing and scarring in patients undergoing oncological surgeries.)<|COMPLETE|>"}{"title": "NUTRICI\u00d3N EN ONCOLOG\u00cdA:NUTRICI\u00d3N EN ONCOLOG\u00cdA is a specialized field of study that addresses the nutritional needs and interventions for cancer patients. This discipline emphasizes the critical importance of screening and diagnosing malnutrition, which can significantly impact patient outcomes. It focuses on the dietary practices and recommendations necessary for cancer patients, particularly during and after treatments such as chemotherapy, hematopoietic cell transplants, and surgical procedures.\n\nThe field recognizes the unique nutritional challenges faced by patients, especially those undergoing treatment for head and neck tumors, and aims to enhance recovery and improve the quality of life through tailored dietary strategies. Nutritional support in oncology encompasses managing the dietary needs of patients before, during, and after treatment, including the implementation of nutritional guidelines and protocols for post-surgical care. This comprehensive approach ensures that cancer patients receive the necessary nutritional interventions to optimize their health and recovery throughout their treatment journey."}{"title": "\u00cdNDICE DE DETSKY:The Detsky index is a nutritional assessment tool used to evaluate the nutritional status of cancer patients."}{"title": "ALTERACIONES CICATRIZACI\u00d3N:Alteraciones cicatrizaci\u00f3n are complications in wound healing that can arise from poor nutritional status in cancer patients."}{"title": "DESCENSO MASA MAGRA:Descenso masa magra refers to the loss of lean body mass, which is a common issue in patients with dysphagia and malnutrition."}{"title": "INCREMENTO DE INFECCIONES:Incremento de infecciones indicates the increased risk of infections due to malnutrition and immunodeficiency in cancer patients."}{"title": "DESCENSO DEL ESTATUS FUNCIONAL:Descenso del estatus funcional refers to the decline in a patient's ability to perform daily activities, often linked to malnutrition."}{"title": "DESCENSO DE LA HABILIDAD DE DEGLUTIR:Descenso de la habilidad de deglutir is a direct consequence of dysphagia, impacting the nutritional intake of patients."}{"title": "ENDOSCOPIA ALTA CON FIBRA \u00d3PTICA:High fiber optic endoscopy is a technique used to evaluate vocal cord function and swallowing dynamics"}{"title": "\u00cdNDICE NUTRICIONAL DE PINATO:The Nutritional Index of Pinato (PNI) is a scoring system used to assess nutritional status based on serum albumin and lymphocyte count"}{"title": "PACIENTES CON TUMORES DE CABEZA Y CUELLO:Patients suffering from head and neck tumors who may experience nutritional challenges and swallowing difficulties"}{"title": "ALTA CONTROL CONSULTA EXTERNA:This refers to the follow-up care and external consultation for patients after treatment for dysphagia."}{"title": "GLOSECTOM\u00cdA TOTAL:A surgical procedure involving the total removal of the tongue, requiring enteral nutrition and careful dietary management post-operation."}{"title": "GLOSECTOM\u00cdA PARCIAL:A surgical procedure involving the partial removal of the tongue, with a typically quicker recovery and tolerance for modified texture foods."}{"title": "LARINGECTOM\u00cdA TOTAL:A surgical procedure involving the total removal of the larynx, necessitating enteral nutrition and gradual transition to oral nutrition."}{"title": "LARINGECTOM\u00cdA PARCIAL:A surgical procedure involving the partial removal of the larynx, requiring careful management of nutrition post-surgery."}{"title": "FARINGOLARINGECTOM\u00cdA:A surgical procedure that combines the removal of the pharynx and larynx, requiring enteral nutrition and careful dietary management."}{"title": "ESOFAGOGASTROPLASTIA:A surgical procedure involving reconstruction of the esophagus and stomach, requiring initial artificial nutrition and gradual transition to oral nutrition."}{"title": "NUTRICI\u00d3N MIXTA:A combination of oral and enteral nutrition, typically used for patients who require additional nutritional support post-surgery."}{"title": "ALITRAQ:Alitraq is a specialized nutritional formula designed for enteral feeding, specifically formulated to meet the needs of patients requiring enteral nutrition. It contains a carefully balanced composition of macronutrients, providing specific caloric and protein content essential for these patients. Alitraq aims to support the nutritional requirements of individuals who cannot consume food orally, ensuring they receive adequate nutrition through enteral means."}{"title": "IMPACT ORAL:Impact Oral is a nutritional formula designed for oral intake, specifically intended for patients who require oral feeding. It serves as a nutritional supplement that provides essential nutrients to support the health and well-being of these individuals."}{"title": "PERATIVE:Perative is a nutritional formula designed to support patients' dietary needs, particularly in surgical and clinical environments. It aims to provide essential nutrients that assist in the recovery and overall health of patients undergoing medical treatments."}{"title": "CUBISON:Cubison is a nutritional product designed to meet the dietary needs of patients requiring dietary management. It serves as a nutritional supplement that provides essential nutrients, specifically aimed at individuals in need of dietary support."}{"title": "CLINUTREN REPAIR:Clinutren Repair is a specialized nutritional formula designed to aid recovery and provide essential nutrients to support healing in patients. This product is specifically formulated to meet the nutritional needs of individuals undergoing recovery, ensuring they receive the necessary components to facilitate their healing process."}{"title": "ARGININA VEGENAT MED:Arginina Vegenat Med is a dietary supplement that provides arginine for patients needing specific nutritional support."}{"title": "ARGININA NM:Arginina NM is a nutritional product that supplies arginine in a liquid form for easier consumption."}{"title": "GLUTAMINA VEGENAT MED:Glutamina Vegenat Med is a dietary supplement providing glutamine for patients requiring additional nutritional support."}{"title": "RESOURCE GLUTAMINA:Resource Glutamina is a brand of glutamine supplements designed to provide nutritional support for patients. The products offered by Resource Glutamina aim to enhance the dietary needs of individuals, ensuring they receive the necessary glutamine to support their health and well-being."}{"title": "NUTRICI\u00d3N EN CIRUG\u00cdA DE TUMORES DE CABEZA Y CUELLO:This event focuses on the nutritional management of patients undergoing surgery for head and neck tumors, emphasizing dietary modifications and support."}{"title": "C\u00c1NCER DE CUELLO:C\u00e1ncer de cuello refers to cancer affecting the neck area, which requires specific nutritional management during treatment."}{"title": "GLUTAMINA VEGANAT MED:Glutamina Vegenat Med is a glutamine product designed for nutritional supplementation in patients."}{"title": "KABI GLUTAMINA:"}{"title": "AMERICAN CANCER SOCIETY:The American Cancer Society is a nationwide voluntary health organization committed to eliminating cancer and enhancing the quality of life for individuals affected by the disease. In addition to its overarching mission, the organization offers specific guidelines regarding the nutritional needs of cancer patients, advising the use of multivitamins during chemotherapy and radiotherapy to support their health during treatment."}{"title": "HEAD AND NECK CANCER:Head and neck cancer refers to a group of cancers that originate in the head and neck region, often requiring specialized treatment and care."}{"title": "DIXON PR:Dixon PR is a researcher involved in studies related to head and neck cancer and its treatment outcomes."}{"title": "COHEN EE:Cohen EE is a researcher who contributed to the American Cancer Society's guidelines on head and neck cancer survivorship care."}{"title": "KLIN ONKOL:Klin Onkol is a journal that publishes research and reviews on clinical oncology, including studies on head and neck cancer."}{"title": "LARYNGEAL CANCER:Laryngeal cancer is a type of cancer that occurs in the larynx (voice box), often requiring specific treatment approaches."}{"title": "EATING ASSESSMENT TOOL:The Eating Assessment Tool (EAT-10) is a validated tool used to assess swallowing difficulties in patients, particularly relevant for those with head and neck cancer."}{"title": "OROPHARYNGEAL DYSPHAGIA:Oropharyngeal dysphagia refers to difficulty swallowing that arises from issues in the oropharynx. This condition is commonly observed in patients who have head and neck cancer, highlighting its association with this specific type of malignancy."}{"title": "GROSSBERG AJ:Grossberg AJ is a researcher who has studied the association of body composition with survival in patients treated for head and neck squamous cell carcinoma."}{"title": "HEAD AND NECK SQUAMOUS CELL CARCINOMA:Head and neck squamous cell carcinoma is a type of cancer that arises from the squamous cells lining the head and neck region."}{"title": "DANAN D:Danan D is a researcher who has studied the prognostic value of albumin in patients with head and neck cancer."}{"title": "FU Y:"}{"title": "ANN OTOL RHINOL LARYNGOL:A medical journal that publishes research related to otolaryngology, including studies on oropharyngeal dysphagia."}{"title": "NAT REV GASTROENTEROL HEPATOL:A journal that focuses on gastroenterology and hepatology, providing reviews and research articles on various topics including dysphagia."}{"title": "AJR AM J ROENTGENOL:A journal that publishes articles related to radiology, including studies on fluoroscopic evaluations of medical conditions."}{"title": "SUPPORT CARE CANCER:Support Care Cancer is a journal dedicated to publishing research on supportive care in cancer treatment. It emphasizes the importance of nutritional therapy for cancer patients and explores various aspects of supportive care, including the nutritional status and overall quality of life of individuals undergoing cancer treatment. The journal serves as a valuable resource for healthcare professionals seeking to improve the well-being of cancer patients through comprehensive supportive care strategies."}{"title": "FLUOROSCOPIC EVALUATION:A diagnostic procedure used to assess oropharyngeal dysphagia, involving real-time imaging to evaluate swallowing mechanics."}{"title": "CANCER PATIENTS:Cancer patients are individuals diagnosed with cancer who are undergoing treatment and may require nutritional support to manage their health. These patients often face various complications related to their condition, including dysphagia, which can further complicate their nutritional needs. As subjects of various studies, cancer patients are also the focus of research aimed at understanding the relationship between nutrition and treatment outcomes. Overall, the care and support of cancer patients encompass a comprehensive approach to address their medical and nutritional challenges during their treatment journey."}{"title": "NEOPLASIAS GASTROINTESTINALES:NEOPLASIAS GASTROINTESTINALES, or gastrointestinal neoplasms, represent a major cause of cancer mortality globally. These neoplasms are a significant health concern, highlighting the importance of nutritional intervention and support in their management. Given their impact on cancer mortality, there is a critical need for nutritional evaluation to aid in the treatment and prevention of these conditions."}{"title": "MALNUTRICI\u00d3N RELACIONADA CON EL C\u00c1NCER:Malnutrition related to cancer refers to the nutritional deficiencies that occur in patients due to the disease and its treatment, impacting their overall health."}{"title": "GRUPO ERAS:El grupo ERAS (Enhanced Recovery After Surgery) proporciona recomendaciones para la recuperaci\u00f3n de pacientes con tumores digestivos."}{"title": "NUTRICIONAL RISK SCREENING 2002:"}{"title": "INMUNONUTRICI\u00d3N:INMUNONUTRICI\u00d3N refers to the study and application of nutrition that influences the immune response, particularly in patients requiring artificial nutritional support. This nutritional approach aims to enhance the immune function of patients, especially those undergoing major surgeries, including surgeries related to gastric cancer. Additionally, immunonutrition is utilized to mitigate the hypermetabolic response to surgery and to promote recovery in these patients. Overall, INMUNONUTRICI\u00d3N plays a crucial role in improving health outcomes for individuals with compromised immune systems due to surgical interventions."}{"title": "COMPLICACIONES POSTOPERATORIAS:Las complicaciones postoperatorias son efectos adversos que pueden surgir despu\u00e9s de la cirug\u00eda, y su incidencia es especialmente alta en pacientes con c\u00e1ncer, como aquellos con c\u00e1ncer de p\u00e1ncreas y otros c\u00e1nceres gastrointestinales. Estas complicaciones pueden ser m\u00e1s frecuentes debido a factores como la malnutrici\u00f3n y la p\u00e9rdida de masa muscular, que son comunes en este grupo de pacientes. Para mitigar estos problemas, se busca implementar un tratamiento nutricional adecuado, lo que puede ayudar a reducir la aparici\u00f3n de complicaciones postoperatorias en estos individuos vulnerables."}{"title": "\u00cdNDICE PRON\u00d3STICO NUTRICIONAL:El \u00edndice pron\u00f3stico nutricional es un indicador que se asocia con el pron\u00f3stico de los pacientes con c\u00e1ncer g\u00e1strico, donde un \u00edndice bajo se relaciona con un pron\u00f3stico desfavorable."}{"title": "NUTRICI\u00d3N PERIOPERATORIA:La nutrici\u00f3n perioperatoria se refiere a la administraci\u00f3n de nutrientes antes y despu\u00e9s de la cirug\u00eda para reducir complicaciones y mejorar la recuperaci\u00f3n."}{"title": "GU\u00cdAS DE LA ESPEN:Las Gu\u00edas de la ESPEN son recomendaciones para la pr\u00e1ctica cl\u00ednica en nutrici\u00f3n, especialmente en pacientes con c\u00e1ncer."}{"title": "KIM ET AL.:Kim et al. son investigadores que realizaron un estudio sobre la comparaci\u00f3n de la nutrici\u00f3n enteral y parenteral en pacientes gastrectomizados."}{"title": "SARCOCENIA:Sarcopenia es la p\u00e9rdida de masa muscular que puede ocurrir en pacientes mayores con c\u00e1ncer, aumentando el riesgo de complicaciones postoperatorias."}{"title": "NEOPLASIAS DIGESTIVAS:Neoplasias digestivas son tumores que afectan el tracto digestivo y pueden requerir cirug\u00eda y tratamiento nutricional."}{"title": "CUIDADO PERIOPERATORIO:"}{"title": "ODINOFAGIA:ODINOFAGIA refers to the pain experienced while swallowing, which significantly impacts patients diagnosed with esophageal cancer. This condition complicates the intake of both food and liquids, making it a challenging symptom for those affected. In the context of esophageal cancer, odinofagia is recognized as a common symptom that can severely hinder the quality of life for patients."}{"title": "INFLAMACI\u00d3N SIST\u00c9MICA:La inflamaci\u00f3n sist\u00e9mica es una respuesta del cuerpo que puede ser provocada por el c\u00e1ncer. Esta condici\u00f3n afecta el metabolismo y puede contribuir a la malnutrici\u00f3n en los pacientes. Adem\u00e1s, se ha observado que la inflamaci\u00f3n sist\u00e9mica est\u00e1 relacionada con la p\u00e9rdida de peso en estos pacientes, lo cual se asocia con niveles elevados de prote\u00edna C-reactiva (PCR)."}{"title": "AUMENTO DEL GASTO ENERG\u00c9TICO:Condici\u00f3n que contribuye a la p\u00e9rdida de peso en pacientes con c\u00e1ncer, relacionada con la caquexia tumoral."}{"title": "TERAPIA NEOADYUVANTE:La terapia neoadyuvante es un tratamiento previo a la cirug\u00eda que combina quimioterapia y/o radioterapia para tratar tumores esof\u00e1gicos, pero puede afectar negativamente el estado nutricional de los pacientes."}{"title": "MORBILIDAD PERIOPERATORIA:La morbilidad perioperatoria se refiere a las complicaciones que pueden ocurrir alrededor del tiempo de una cirug\u00eda, especialmente en pacientes con c\u00e1ncer esof\u00e1gico."}{"title": "QUIMIOTERAPIA NEADYUVANTE:La quimioterapia neoadyuvante es un tratamiento que se aplica antes de la cirug\u00eda para reducir el tama\u00f1o del tumor y mejorar los resultados quir\u00fargicos."}{"title": "QUIMIORADIOTERAPIA:La quimiorradioterapia es un tratamiento combinado de quimioterapia y radioterapia que se utiliza para tratar el c\u00e1ncer, pero puede empeorar la disfagia en los pacientes."}{"title": "NECESIDADES CAL\u00d3RICAS Y PROTEICAS:Las necesidades cal\u00f3ricas y proteicas son esenciales para el manejo nutricional de pacientes con c\u00e1ncer, variando seg\u00fan su estado f\u00edsico y tratamiento."}{"title": "SARCOMENIA:"}{"title": "ESOFAGECTOM\u00cdA:ESOFAGECTOM\u00cdA is a surgical procedure that involves the removal of part or all of the esophagus, primarily performed to treat esophageal cancer. This invasive surgical intervention is specifically designed for patients diagnosed with esophageal cancer, aiming to eliminate the affected tissue. The procedure can vary in extent, depending on the severity of the cancer, and is a critical option in the management of this serious condition."}{"title": "NUTRICI\u00d3N ENTERAL PRECOZ:La nutrici\u00f3n enteral precoz se refiere a la administraci\u00f3n temprana de nutrientes a trav\u00e9s de un tubo en pacientes postoperatorios, lo que puede mejorar la recuperaci\u00f3n intestinal y reducir complicaciones."}{"title": "COMPLICACIONES POSTQUIR\u00daRGICAS:Las complicaciones postquir\u00fargicas son problemas de salud que pueden surgir despu\u00e9s de una cirug\u00eda, como infecciones o problemas de cicatrizaci\u00f3n, especialmente relevantes en pacientes con c\u00e1ncer de es\u00f3fago."}{"title": "GASTROSTOM\u00cdA ENDOSC\u00d3PICA:GASTROSTOM\u00cdA ENDOSC\u00d3PICA es un procedimiento m\u00e9dico dise\u00f1ado para proporcionar nutrici\u00f3n enteral a largo plazo a pacientes que no pueden tragar adecuadamente. Este procedimiento se lleva a cabo bajo anestesia local y presenta una menor morbimortalidad en comparaci\u00f3n con la gastrostom\u00eda quir\u00fargica. Consiste en la colocaci\u00f3n de un tubo de alimentaci\u00f3n en el est\u00f3mago a trav\u00e9s de la piel, lo que permite mantener el aporte nutricional necesario para aquellos que requieren asistencia alimentaria."}{"title": "PACIENTES CON C\u00c1NCER:\"PACIENTES CON C\u00c1NCER\" refers to individuals diagnosed with cancer, who often face various health challenges, including complications related to nutrition and surgical interventions. These patients may require specialized nutritional support to help maintain their health during treatment. Specifically, cancer patients receiving Nutritional Education and Development (NED) benefit from tailored nutritional assistance aimed at enhancing their overall well-being throughout their treatment journey."}{"title": "ESOFAECTOM\u00cdA:"}{"title": "COMPLICACIONES PULMONARES:Las complicaciones pulmonares son efectos adversos que pueden ocurrir en pacientes despu\u00e9s de la cirug\u00eda, afectando su recuperaci\u00f3n y estado de salud."}{"title": "DEHISCENCIA ANASTOM\u00d3TICA:La dehiscencia anastom\u00f3tica es una complicaci\u00f3n grave que ocurre cuando una sutura en una anastomosis quir\u00fargica se abre, lo que puede llevar a infecciones y otras complicaciones."}{"title": "ESTANCIA EN UCI:La estancia en UCI se refiere al tiempo que un paciente pasa en la Unidad de Cuidados Intensivos, donde se brinda atenci\u00f3n m\u00e9dica intensiva."}{"title": "INFECCIONES DE LA HERIDA:Las infecciones de la herida son complicaciones que pueden surgir despu\u00e9s de una cirug\u00eda, afectando la recuperaci\u00f3n del paciente."}{"title": "DUODENOPANCREATECTOM\u00cdA CEF\u00c1LICA:La duodenopancreatectom\u00eda cef\u00e1lica es un procedimiento quir\u00fargico est\u00e1ndar para el tratamiento de tumores en la cabeza del p\u00e1ncreas y tiene complicaciones nutricionales significativas."}{"title": "DIFICULTADES ALIMENTARIAS:Las dificultades alimentarias son un s\u00edntoma com\u00fan en pacientes con c\u00e1ncer, que pueden experimentar anorexia y otros problemas relacionados con la ingesta."}{"title": "CRIBADO MUST:El cribado MUST (Malnutrition Universal Screening Tool) es una herramienta utilizada para evaluar la malnutrici\u00f3n y su impacto en la morbilidad postoperatoria."}{"title": "\u00cdNDICE DE RIESGO NUTRICIONAL:El \u00cdndice de Riesgo Nutricional (IRN) es una herramienta que muestra concordancia en relaci\u00f3n con la morbilidad global en pacientes con c\u00e1ncer."}{"title": "QUIMIO O QUIMIORRADIOTERAPIA:La quimio o quimiorradioterapia de inducci\u00f3n es un tratamiento que algunos pacientes con c\u00e1ncer de p\u00e1ncreas reciben antes de la cirug\u00eda."}{"title": "INMUNONUTRICI\u00d3N ENTERAL:La inmunonutrici\u00f3n enteral es un tipo de nutrici\u00f3n que se asocia con beneficios en la respuesta inmune y la recuperaci\u00f3n postoperatoria en pacientes con c\u00e1ncer."}{"title": "ESTRATEGIA ERAS:La estrategia ERAS (Enhanced Recovery After Surgery) es un enfoque que busca mejorar la recuperaci\u00f3n postoperatoria de los pacientes."}{"title": "RESECCI\u00d3N TIPO WHIPPLE:La resecci\u00f3n tipo Whipple es un procedimiento quir\u00fargico espec\u00edfico para tratar el c\u00e1ncer pancre\u00e1tico."}{"title": "RECUENTO LINFOCITARIO:El recuento linfocitario es un indicador de la respuesta inmune en pacientes, que puede verse afectado por la nutrici\u00f3n."}{"title": "D\u00cdA 3 POSTOPERATORIO:El d\u00eda 3 postoperatorio es un momento clave para evaluar la respuesta inmune y el estado de los pacientes tras la cirug\u00eda."}{"title": "D\u00cdA 7 POSTOPERATORIO:El d\u00eda 7 postoperatorio es un momento importante para observar la recuperaci\u00f3n y los efectos de la nutrici\u00f3n en pacientes."}{"title": "NUTRICI\u00d3N EST\u00c1NDAR:NUTRICI\u00d3N EST\u00c1NDAR se refiere al tipo de nutrici\u00f3n que se est\u00e1 administrando a un var\u00f3n de 75 a\u00f1os. Esta nutrici\u00f3n tiene una concentraci\u00f3n de 1 kcal/ml y contiene un 16% de prote\u00ednas."}{"title": "CIRUG\u00cdA PANCRE\u00c1TICA:CIRUG\u00cdA PANCRE\u00c1TICA encompasses various surgical procedures performed on the pancreas, including Whipple surgery, to treat conditions such as cancer."}{"title": "HEPATECTOM\u00cdA:HEPATECTOM\u00cdA is a surgical procedure that involves the removal of a portion of the liver, often performed for liver cancer or other liver diseases."}{"title": "CIRUG\u00cdA BILIAR:CIRUG\u00cdA BILIAR refers to surgical procedures related to the bile ducts and gallbladder, often performed to treat gallstones or bile duct obstructions."}{"title": "WHIPPLE:"}{"title": "C\u00c1NCER GASTROINTESTINAL:Cancer affecting the gastrointestinal tract, which has low survival rates and requires careful nutritional management."}{"title": "QUIMIO Y/O RADIOTERAPIA:Chemotherapy and/or radiotherapy are treatments that can complicate the nutritional status of patients with gastrointestinal tumors."}{"title": "GERIATRIC FRAILTY:A condition that, along with nutritional status, is assessed to predict postoperative mortality in gastric cancer surgery."}{"title": "PREOPERATIVE IMMUNONUTRITION:A nutritional strategy applied before surgery to improve outcomes for patients undergoing gastrointestinal surgery."}{"title": "JOURNAL OF GASTROINTESTINAL SURGERY:A publication that features research and studies related to gastrointestinal surgery, including nutritional aspects."}{"title": "JOURNAL OF PARENTERAL AND ENTERAL NUTRITION:The Journal of Parenteral and Enteral Nutrition is a specialized publication dedicated to the dissemination of research and guidelines concerning parenteral and enteral nutrition. It serves as a vital resource for healthcare professionals by focusing on the latest findings and best practices related to nutritional support for patients. Through its publications, the journal aims to enhance the understanding and application of nutritional therapies in clinical settings."}{"title": "JOURNAL OF GASTROENTEROLOGY AND HEPATOLOGY:A journal that covers research related to gastroenterology, including nutritional studies for gastric cancer patients."}{"title": "BODY MASS INDEX:Body Mass Index (BMI) is a significant measure that assesses nutritional status and can influence perioperative outcomes and survival rates following gastric cancer resection. It serves as an important indicator in evaluating the health and nutritional condition of individuals, particularly in the context of cancer outcomes."}{"title": "NUTRITIONAL INDEX:The prognostic nutritional index is a tool used to predict the biological aggressiveness of gastric carcinoma."}{"title": "YONSEI MEDICAL JOURNAL:The Yonsei Medical Journal is a peer-reviewed medical journal that covers various aspects of medical research and clinical practices."}{"title": "INTERNATIONAL JOURNAL OF SURGERY:The International Journal of Surgery publishes research on surgical techniques and outcomes across various specialties."}{"title": "ANNALS OF SURGICAL ONCOLOGY:The \"Annals of Surgical Oncology\" is a peer-reviewed medical journal dedicated to the field of surgical oncology. It publishes a wide range of research studies related to cancer surgery, including specific investigations into esophageal cancer and its treatment. The journal serves as a significant resource for professionals in the field, contributing to the advancement of knowledge and practices in surgical oncology."}{"title": "AMERICAN JOURNAL OF SURGERY:The American Journal of Surgery is a peer-reviewed journal that publishes articles on surgical techniques and outcomes."}{"title": "TOTAL GASTRECTOMY:Total gastrectomy is a surgical procedure involving the removal of the entire stomach, often performed on patients with gastric cancer."}{"title": "EARLY ORAL FEEDING:Early oral feeding refers to the practice of allowing patients to eat soon after surgery, which is studied for its effects on recovery."}{"title": "ENTERAL IMMUNONUTRITION:Enteral immunonutrition is a nutritional support strategy used in patients undergoing surgery, particularly for cancer treatment."}{"title": "CHEONG JH:Cheong JH is a co-author of a study on perioperative nutritional status changes in gastrointestinal cancer patients published in the Yonsei Medical Journal."}{"title": "LEE KY:Lee KY is a co-author of a study on perioperative nutritional status changes in gastrointestinal cancer patients published in the Yonsei Medical Journal."}{"title": "LEE H:Lee H is a co-author of a study on perioperative nutritional status changes in gastrointestinal cancer patients published in the Yonsei Medical Journal."}{"title": "LEE JG:Lee JG is a co-author of a study on perioperative nutritional status changes in gastrointestinal cancer patients published in the Yonsei Medical Journal."}{"title": "NOH SH:Noh SH is a co-author of a study on perioperative nutritional status changes in gastrointestinal cancer patients published in the Yonsei Medical Journal."}{"title": "HUR H:Hur H is an author of a pilot study on the effects of early oral feeding on surgical outcomes after curative surgery for gastric cancer published in the World Journal of Surgery."}{"title": "SI Y:Si Y is a co-author of a pilot study on the effects of early oral feeding on surgical outcomes after curative surgery for gastric cancer published in the World Journal of Surgery."}{"title": "KANG WK:Kang WK is a co-author of a pilot study on the effects of early oral feeding on surgical outcomes after curative surgery for gastric cancer published in the World Journal of Surgery."}{"title": "KIM W:Kim W is a co-author of a pilot study on the effects of early oral feeding on surgical outcomes after curative surgery for gastric cancer published in the World Journal of Surgery."}{"title": "JEON HM:Jeon HM is a co-author of a pilot study on the effects of early oral feeding on surgical outcomes after curative surgery for gastric cancer published in the World Journal of Surgery."}{"title": "HIRA M:Hira M is an author of a study on patient-controlled dietary schedules improving clinical outcomes after gastrectomy for gastric cancer published in the World Journal of Surgery."}{"title": "TSUJINAKA T:Tsujinaka T is a co-author of a study on patient-controlled dietary schedules improving clinical outcomes after gastrectomy for gastric cancer published in the World Journal of Surgery."}{"title": "TAKENO A:Takeno A is a co-author of a study on patient-controlled dietary schedules improving clinical outcomes after gastrectomy for gastric cancer published in the World Journal of Surgery."}{"title": "FUJITANI K:Fujitani K is a co-author of a study on patient-controlled dietary schedules improving clinical outcomes after gastrectomy for gastric cancer published in the World Journal of Surgery."}{"title": "KURATA M:Kurata M is a co-author of a study on patient-controlled dietary schedules improving clinical outcomes after gastrectomy for gastric cancer published in the World Journal of Surgery."}{"title": "HONG L:Hong L is an author of a study on the effect of early oral feeding on short-term outcomes of patients receiving laparoscopic distal gastrectomy published in the International Journal of Surgery."}{"title": "ZHAO Q:Zhao Q is a co-author of a study on the effect of early oral feeding on short-term outcomes of patients receiving laparoscopic distal gastrectomy published in the International Journal of Surgery."}{"title": "KAMEI H:Kamei H is an author of a study on the quick recovery of serum diamine oxidase activity in patients undergoing total gastrectomy published in the American Journal of Surgery."}{"title": "HACHISUKA T:Hachisuka T is a co-author of a study on the quick recovery of serum diamine oxidase activity in patients undergoing total gastrectomy published in the American Journal of Surgery."}{"title": "NAKAO M:Nakao M is a co-author of a study on the quick recovery of serum diamine oxidase activity in patients undergoing total gastrectomy published in the American Journal of Surgery."}{"title": "TAKAGI K:Takagi K is a co-author of a study on the quick recovery of serum diamine oxidase activity in patients undergoing total gastrectomy published in the American Journal of Surgery."}{"title": "SIERZEGA M:Sierzega M is a researcher focused on the field of immunonutrition and its impact on surgical outcomes. Additionally, Sierzega M has authored a study that examines the feasibility and outcomes of early oral feeding following total gastrectomy for cancer, which was published in the Journal of Gastrointestinal Surgery."}{"title": "CHORUZ R:Choruz R is a co-author of a study on the feasibility and outcomes of early oral feeding after total gastrectomy for cancer published in the Journal of Gastrointestinal Surgery."}{"title": "PIETRUSZKA S:Pietruszka S is a co-author of a study on the feasibility and outcomes of early oral feeding after total gastrectomy for cancer published in the Journal of Gastrointestinal Surgery."}{"title": "KULIG P:Kulig P is a co-author of a study on the feasibility and outcomes of early oral feeding after total gastrectomy for cancer published in the Journal of Gastrointestinal Surgery."}{"title": "KOLODZIEJCZYK P:Kolodziejczyk P is a co-author of a study on the feasibility and outcomes of early oral feeding after total gastrectomy for cancer published in the Journal of Gastrointestinal Surgery."}{"title": "KULIG J:Kulig J is a co-author of a study on the feasibility and outcomes of early oral feeding after total gastrectomy for cancer published in the Journal of Gastrointestinal Surgery."}{"title": "GABOR S:Gabor S is an author of a study comparing early enteral feeding with parenteral nutrition after esophageal or esophagogastric resection published in the British Journal of Nutrition."}{"title": "RENNER H:Renner H is a co-author of a study comparing early enteral feeding with parenteral nutrition after esophageal or esophagogastric resection published in the British Journal of Nutrition."}{"title": "MATZI V:Matzi V is a co-author of a study comparing early enteral feeding with parenteral nutrition after esophageal or esophagogastric resection published in the British Journal of Nutrition."}{"title": "RATZENHOFER B:Ratzenhofer B is a co-author of a study comparing early enteral feeding with parenteral nutrition after esophageal or esophagogastric resection published in the British Journal of Nutrition."}{"title": "LINDENMANN J:Lindenmann J is a co-author of a study comparing early enteral feeding with parenteral nutrition after esophageal or esophagogastric re"}{"title": "ASIAN J SURG:Asian J Surg is a journal that publishes research related to surgical practices and outcomes, including studies on gastric cancer surgery."}{"title": "MINERVA GASTROENTEROL DIETOL:Minerva Gastroenterol Dietol is a journal focusing on gastrointestinal health and nutrition, featuring studies on enteral nutrition in postoperative patients."}{"title": "INT J CLIN EXP MED:International Journal of Clinical and Experimental Medicine publishes research on clinical practices, including studies on nutrition after gastrointestinal surgeries."}{"title": "J INVESTIG MED:Journal of Investigative Medicine publishes research on medical investigations, including systematic reviews on nutrition after abdominal surgeries."}{"title": "GENET MOL RES:Genetics and Molecular Research is a journal that publishes studies on genetics and molecular biology, including research on nutritional impacts post-surgery."}{"title": "KOREAN J GASTROENTEROL:Korean Journal of Gastroenterology publishes research on gastrointestinal diseases and treatments, including studies on nutrition after gastrectomy."}{"title": "DGEM:German Society for Nutritional Medicine focuses on nutritional practices and guidelines, including those relevant to surgical patients."}{"title": "HANG L:Hang L is an author involved in the study of early enteral immunonutrition in postoperative gastric cancer patients."}{"title": "SHUI SY:Shui SY is an author who co-authored a meta-analysis on enteral immunonutrition in gastric cancer patients."}{"title": "HUANG D:Huang D is an author who researched early enteral nutrition in elderly patients after gastrointestinal cancer surgery."}{"title": "SUN Z:Sun Z is an author who contributed to the study on early enteral nutrition in elderly patients post-surgery."}{"title": "ZHAO XF:Zhao XF is an author who conducted a systematic review on enteral versus parenteral nutrition after major abdominal surgery."}{"title": "WU N:Wu N is an author involved in the systematic review comparing enteral and parenteral nutrition after surgery."}{"title": "ZHAO GQ:Zhao GQ is an author who contributed to the research on nutritional support after major abdominal surgery."}{"title": "LI B:Li B is an author who studied the impact of early enteral and parenteral nutrition on clinical outcomes after gastric surgery."}{"title": "LIU HY:Liu HY is an author who co-authored research on nutritional support in gastric cancer patients."}{"title": "GUO SH:Guo SH is an author involved in the study of nutritional impacts post-gastric surgery."}{"title": "SUN P:Sun P is an author who contributed to research on early postoperative enteral nutrition in gastric cancer patients."}{"title": "GONG FM:Gong FM is an author who studied the effects of early enteral nutrition on clinical outcomes in gastric cancer patients."}{"title": "RYAN AM:Ryan AM is an author who researched the nutritional implications of total gastrectomy for malignancy."}{"title": "HEALY LA:Healy LA is an author who contributed to the study on nutritional support after total gastrectomy."}{"title": "POWER DG:Power DG is an author involved in research on the impact of parenteral nutritional support after surgery."}{"title": "ROWLEY SP:Rowley SP is an author who studied the short-term nutritional implications of total gastrectomy."}{"title": "REYNOLDS JV:Reynolds JV is an author who contributed to research on nutritional support after gastric surgery."}{"title": "WEI Z:Wei Z is an author who conducted a study on omega-3 fish oil fat emulsion-based parenteral nutrition for surgical patients."}{"title": "WANG W:Wang W is an author involved in research on parenteral nutrition following surgical resection of gastric tumors."}{"title": "CHEN J:Chen J is an author who contributed to the study of nutritional support in patients after gastric surgery."}{"title": "YANG D:Yang D is an author who researched the effects of nutritional support in surgical patients."}{"title": "YAN R:Yan R is an author involved in the study of parenteral nutrition for patients after gastric surgery."}{"title": "CAI Q:Cai Q is an author who contributed to research on nutritional support following surgical resection of gastric tumors."}{"title": "WU GH:Wu GH is an author who studied perioperative artificial nutrition in malnourished gastrointestinal cancer patients."}{"title": "LIU ZH:Liu ZH is an author involved in research on artificial nutrition in gastrointestinal cancer patients."}{"title": "WU ZH:Wu ZH is an author who contributed to studies on nutritional support in surgical patients."}{"title": "WU ZG:Wu ZG is an author involved in research on artificial nutrition in malnourished patients."}{"title": "BODOKY G:Bodoky G is a researcher and author who has made significant contributions to the ESPEN Guidelines on Enteral Nutrition and nutritional support in oncology. Through their work, Bodoky G has played a vital role in shaping guidelines that inform best practices in nutritional care for patients, particularly in the context of oncology."}{"title": "FEARON K:Fearon K is an author involved in the ESPEN Guidelines on nutritional support in cancer patients."}{"title": "SELGA G:Selga G is an author involved in the ESPEN Guidelines on nutritional support in oncology."}{"title": "KOZAR R:Kozar R is an author involved in the recommendations from the North American Surgical Nutrition Summit."}{"title": "MARTINDALE RG:Martindale RG is an author recognized for their contributions to the field of nutrition, particularly in the context of surgical care. They played a significant role in the consensus recommendations from the North American Surgical Nutrition Summit, which focuses on best practices in nutritional support. Additionally, Martindale RG is one of the authors involved in developing guidelines for nutrition support therapy specifically aimed at critically ill patients, highlighting their expertise and commitment to improving patient outcomes through effective nutritional strategies."}{"title": "DROVER JW:Drover JW is an author who contributed to the consensus recommendations from the North American Surgical Nutrition Summit."}{"title": "FLUM D:Flum D is an author involved in the recommendations from the North American Surgical Nutrition Summit."}{"title": "KO C:Ko C is an author who contributed to the consensus recommendations from the North American Surgical Nutrition Summit."}{"title": "KUDSK KA:Kudsk KA is a researcher known for conducting trials on enteral diets and their effects on septic complications. In addition to